1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,960
Listen, practice, speak, practice makes you perfect.

2
00:00:13,960 --> 00:00:14,960
Hi everyone.

3
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:17,480
Welcome to today's English Conversation Practice.

4
00:00:17,480 --> 00:00:18,680
I'm Daniel.

5
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:22,840
And I'm Sophia, and we are so happy you're here with us today.

6
00:00:22,840 --> 00:00:28,280
On this podcast, we help you speak English naturally, confidently, and professionally in

7
00:00:28,280 --> 00:00:30,520
real life situations.

8
00:00:30,520 --> 00:00:35,000
Today's topic is incredibly useful for anyone working in an office or planning to work

9
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:36,000
in one.

10
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,040
going to talk about how to talk with co-workers in English.

11
00:00:39,040 --> 00:00:40,040
Yes.

12
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:44,760
This is something you do every single day at work, talking with your co-workers.

13
00:00:44,760 --> 00:00:50,360
From saying good morning to asking for help, chatting during lunch, and even handling small

14
00:00:50,360 --> 00:00:54,800
misunderstandings, communication is everywhere.

15
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:59,520
And sometimes it's not about using perfect English, it's about using the right phrases

16
00:00:59,520 --> 00:01:03,200
in the right situation and sounding natural and friendly.

17
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:04,440
Exactly.

18
00:01:04,440 --> 00:01:10,040
So today, we're going to walk through many real-life conversations, practical examples,

19
00:01:10,040 --> 00:01:13,080
and useful phrases that you can start using right away.

20
00:01:13,080 --> 00:01:17,160
Alright, Sophia, let's get started with a typical work day.

21
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:19,120
Imagine you just walked into the office.

22
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:21,680
What's the first thing you say to your coworkers?

23
00:01:21,680 --> 00:01:24,180
The first thing is always a greeting.

24
00:01:24,180 --> 00:01:28,000
You can say, good morning, which is polite and professional.

25
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:31,520
Or you can say, morning, which is a bit more casual.

26
00:01:31,520 --> 00:01:35,120
I usually say, hey, good morning to people I know well.

27
00:01:35,120 --> 00:01:36,560
That's perfect.

28
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:40,120
And after that, we usually ask a simple question like,

29
00:01:40,120 --> 00:01:42,560
how are you or how's it going?

30
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:44,920
Right, let's practice a quick example.

31
00:01:44,920 --> 00:01:47,160
Hey, Sophia, good morning, how's it going?

32
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:48,660
Good morning, Daniel.

33
00:01:48,660 --> 00:01:50,320
It's going well, thanks.

34
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:52,320
I'm feeling pretty productive today.

35
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:53,240
How about you?

36
00:01:53,240 --> 00:01:55,320
I'm doing okay, just a little sleepy.

37
00:01:55,320 --> 00:01:57,320
I didn't get enough rest last night.

38
00:01:57,320 --> 00:01:58,800
That's very natural.

39
00:01:58,800 --> 00:02:01,480
See, you don't have to say something complicated

40
00:02:01,480 --> 00:02:03,520
Just keep it simple and friendly.

41
00:02:03,520 --> 00:02:05,440
What if someone doesn't feel great?

42
00:02:05,440 --> 00:02:06,800
Should they be honest?

43
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:09,060
Yes, but keep it light.

44
00:02:09,060 --> 00:02:10,800
You can say something like,

45
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:12,680
I'm a bit tired today,

46
00:02:12,680 --> 00:02:15,680
or I've got a lot on my plate.

47
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:18,880
That sounds natural and professional at the same time.

48
00:02:18,880 --> 00:02:20,200
Exactly.

49
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:21,720
Now, after greetings,

50
00:02:21,720 --> 00:02:24,640
we usually move into small talk.

51
00:02:24,640 --> 00:02:26,740
Ah, yes, small talk.

52
00:02:26,740 --> 00:02:29,200
The thing that makes many people nervous.

53
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:31,360
But it doesn't have to be difficult.

54
00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:33,600
Let's try a simple example.

55
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:35,680
Daniel, how was your weekend?

56
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:36,960
It was great, actually.

57
00:02:36,960 --> 00:02:39,700
I spent some time with my family and watched a movie.

58
00:02:39,700 --> 00:02:40,760
What about you?

59
00:02:40,760 --> 00:02:42,560
Mine was relaxing.

60
00:02:42,560 --> 00:02:45,560
I didn't do much, just stayed home and read a book.

61
00:02:45,560 --> 00:02:46,960
See how easy that is?

62
00:02:46,960 --> 00:02:50,480
One question, a short answer, and then you ask back.

63
00:02:50,480 --> 00:02:51,720
Exactly.

64
00:02:51,720 --> 00:02:53,640
That's the key to small talk.

65
00:02:53,640 --> 00:02:55,920
Keep it short and balanced.

66
00:02:55,920 --> 00:02:59,440
What are some other safe topics for small talk at work?

67
00:02:59,440 --> 00:03:01,560
the weather is always a good one.

68
00:03:01,560 --> 00:03:04,280
For example, it's really sunny today

69
00:03:04,280 --> 00:03:07,360
or it's so cold this morning.

70
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:10,480
Or even something like, looks like it might rain later.

71
00:03:10,480 --> 00:03:13,760
Yes, and another common topic is food.

72
00:03:13,760 --> 00:03:16,400
You can say, what are you having for lunch?

73
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:19,200
Or that smells really good.

74
00:03:19,200 --> 00:03:21,760
I like that one, food always works.

75
00:03:21,760 --> 00:03:25,160
Now let's move to a very common situation,

76
00:03:25,160 --> 00:03:27,320
asking coworkers for help.

77
00:03:27,320 --> 00:03:29,080
This is something we all need to do,

78
00:03:29,080 --> 00:03:31,320
especially when we're new at a job.

79
00:03:31,320 --> 00:03:34,240
Right, the key here is to be polite.

80
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:38,320
You can start with, excuse me, or do you have a minute?

81
00:03:38,320 --> 00:03:39,760
Let's try an example.

82
00:03:39,760 --> 00:03:41,480
Sophia, do you have a minute?

83
00:03:41,480 --> 00:03:42,840
Sure, what's up?

84
00:03:42,840 --> 00:03:44,800
I'm having trouble with this report.

85
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:46,960
Could you help me understand this section?

86
00:03:46,960 --> 00:03:49,000
Of course, I'd be happy to help.

87
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:50,280
Let's take a look.

88
00:03:50,280 --> 00:03:51,920
That sounds very natural.

89
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:54,520
What if you're busy and can't help right away?

90
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:56,560
Then you can say something like,

91
00:03:56,560 --> 00:03:58,080
I'm a bit busy right now,

92
00:03:58,080 --> 00:04:00,600
but I can help you later, is that okay?

93
00:04:00,600 --> 00:04:02,440
That's polite and honest.

94
00:04:02,440 --> 00:04:05,640
Yes, and it shows respect for both your time

95
00:04:05,640 --> 00:04:07,740
and the other person's needs.

96
00:04:07,740 --> 00:04:09,840
Now, let's flip the situation.

97
00:04:09,840 --> 00:04:12,200
What if someone asks you for help?

98
00:04:12,200 --> 00:04:16,960
You can respond with, sure, of course, or no problem.

99
00:04:16,960 --> 00:04:19,480
Or even let me see how I can help.

100
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:20,800
Exactly.

101
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:25,000
Now let's talk about casual conversations during breaks.

102
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:27,320
Like in the kitchen or coffee area.

103
00:04:27,320 --> 00:04:31,360
Yes, these are great opportunities to build relationships.

104
00:04:31,360 --> 00:04:34,360
For example, you might say, taking a break?

105
00:04:34,360 --> 00:04:37,040
Or I really needed this coffee today.

106
00:04:37,040 --> 00:04:39,280
Let's try a short conversation.

107
00:04:39,280 --> 00:04:41,320
Hey, Sophia, grabbing some coffee?

108
00:04:41,320 --> 00:04:43,240
Yes, I needed a break.

109
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:45,120
It's been a busy morning.

110
00:04:45,120 --> 00:04:45,960
Same here.

111
00:04:45,960 --> 00:04:47,920
I've had back-to-back meetings.

112
00:04:47,920 --> 00:04:49,520
That sounds exhausting.

113
00:04:49,520 --> 00:04:51,960
Hopefully the afternoon will be calmer.

114
00:04:51,960 --> 00:04:53,360
I hope so too.

115
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:56,800
See, that's a natural, friendly conversation.

116
00:04:56,800 --> 00:05:01,920
Now let's talk about meetings. Meetings can be challenging, especially in English.

117
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:06,800
Yes, but there are some simple phrases that can help you feel more confident.

118
00:05:06,800 --> 00:05:10,960
For example, when you want to speak, you can say, can I add something?

119
00:05:10,960 --> 00:05:13,660
Or I'd like to share an idea.

120
00:05:13,660 --> 00:05:15,880
What about interrupting politely?

121
00:05:15,880 --> 00:05:19,240
You can say, sorry to interrupt, but...

122
00:05:19,240 --> 00:05:20,680
Let's try an example.

123
00:05:20,680 --> 00:05:21,680
Sure.

124
00:05:21,680 --> 00:05:25,080
I think we should focus more on marketing strategies.

125
00:05:25,080 --> 00:05:29,720
to interrupt, but I think we should also consider customer feedback.

126
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:32,360
That's a great example of polite interruption.

127
00:05:32,360 --> 00:05:35,800
Now, what if you disagree with someone?

128
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:36,800
That's tricky.

129
00:05:36,800 --> 00:05:42,560
Yes, but you can say, I see your point, but I think…

130
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:44,960
Or that's interesting, however.

131
00:05:44,960 --> 00:05:45,960
Let's try it.

132
00:05:45,960 --> 00:05:48,160
I believe we should increase the budget.

133
00:05:48,160 --> 00:05:53,680
I see your point, but I think we should first review our current spending.

134
00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:55,920
That sounds respectful and professional.

135
00:05:55,920 --> 00:05:56,920
Exactly.

136
00:05:56,920 --> 00:05:59,880
Now, let's talk about emails.

137
00:05:59,880 --> 00:06:02,680
Emails are a big part of workplace communication.

138
00:06:02,680 --> 00:06:03,680
Yes.

139
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:08,520
When you start an email, you can say hi name or hello name.

140
00:06:08,520 --> 00:06:11,120
And for a more formal tone, dear name.

141
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:12,120
Right.

142
00:06:12,120 --> 00:06:16,040
Then you can write something like, I hope you're doing well.

143
00:06:16,040 --> 00:06:18,440
Or I'm writing to follow up on.

144
00:06:18,440 --> 00:06:23,640
And to end the email, you can say best regards or simply thanks.

145
00:06:23,640 --> 00:06:26,240
Let's talk about making plans with co-workers.

146
00:06:26,240 --> 00:06:29,820
Yes, this is important for building relationships.

147
00:06:29,820 --> 00:06:35,000
You can say, do you want to grab lunch or are you free for coffee later?

148
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:36,640
Let's try a quick example.

149
00:06:36,640 --> 00:06:37,640
Sure.

150
00:06:37,640 --> 00:06:39,920
Hey, Sophia, do you want to grab lunch today?

151
00:06:39,920 --> 00:06:42,480
I'd love to, but I have a meeting.

152
00:06:42,480 --> 00:06:43,480
Maybe tomorrow.

153
00:06:43,480 --> 00:06:44,480
Sounds good.

154
00:06:44,480 --> 00:06:45,480
Let's do tomorrow.

155
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:47,920
That's a perfect example.

156
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:50,360
Now let's talk about giving compliments.

157
00:06:50,360 --> 00:06:54,720
Yes, compliments are great for building positive relationships.

158
00:06:54,720 --> 00:06:58,200
You can say, great job on that presentation.

159
00:06:58,200 --> 00:07:01,000
Or I really liked your idea in the meeting.

160
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:03,080
And when someone compliments you?

161
00:07:03,080 --> 00:07:06,320
Just say thank you or I appreciate that.

162
00:07:06,320 --> 00:07:07,840
Simple and effective.

163
00:07:07,840 --> 00:07:11,180
Now let's talk about apologizing.

164
00:07:11,180 --> 00:07:12,520
Very important.

165
00:07:12,520 --> 00:07:18,520
You can say, I'm sorry for the delay or I apologize for the mistake.

166
00:07:18,520 --> 00:07:20,560
And keep the explanation short.

167
00:07:20,560 --> 00:07:22,960
Yes, don't over-explain.

168
00:07:22,960 --> 00:07:26,240
Finally, let's talk about ending the day.

169
00:07:26,240 --> 00:07:29,600
When you leave, you can say, I'm heading out.

170
00:07:29,600 --> 00:07:31,240
Or see you tomorrow.

171
00:07:31,240 --> 00:07:34,240
And on Fridays, have a great weekend!

172
00:07:34,240 --> 00:07:37,120
This has been such a helpful conversation, Sophia.

173
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:42,620
Yes, and remember everyone, the key is to be polite, friendly, and natural when talking

174
00:07:42,620 --> 00:07:44,120
with coworkers.

175
00:07:44,120 --> 00:07:47,320
Keep practicing these phrases every day at work.

176
00:07:47,320 --> 00:07:50,800
The more you practice, the more confident you will become.

177
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:52,840
Thank you so much for listening.

178
00:07:52,840 --> 00:07:54,400
See you in the next episode.

179
00:07:54,400 --> 00:07:55,960
Goodbye, everyone.

180
00:07:55,960 --> 00:07:56,960
Bye.

181
00:07:56,960 --> 00:07:59,400
Welcome back to Business English Learning.

182
00:07:59,400 --> 00:08:00,680
Hi, everyone.

183
00:08:00,680 --> 00:08:03,640
Welcome to today's English Conversation Practice.

184
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:08,260
And we are here to help you speak English naturally, confidently, and professionally

185
00:08:08,260 --> 00:08:10,040
with your coworkers.

186
00:08:10,040 --> 00:08:14,800
Today's topic is how to talk with coworkers in English, and we're going to give you

187
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:21,440
a long, detailed, real-life conversation that covers many situations you face every day at work.

188
00:08:22,160 --> 00:08:28,000
Exactly. You'll hear natural conversations, practical examples, and useful expressions

189
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:30,320
all inside one continuous dialogue.

190
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:35,280
So imagine you're in the office with us. Let's begin our workday.

191
00:08:35,840 --> 00:08:38,240
Good morning, Sophia. How are you today?

192
00:08:38,240 --> 00:08:41,360
Good morning, Daniel. I'm doing really well. Thank you.

193
00:08:41,360 --> 00:08:44,960
I actually had a very productive morning before coming to work.

194
00:08:44,960 --> 00:08:45,960
How about you?

195
00:08:45,960 --> 00:08:46,960
I'm doing okay.

196
00:08:46,960 --> 00:08:49,260
I feel a bit tired, to be honest.

197
00:08:49,260 --> 00:08:51,160
I didn't sleep very well last night.

198
00:08:51,160 --> 00:08:53,160
Oh no, what happened?

199
00:08:53,160 --> 00:08:55,460
I stayed up too late working on a project.

200
00:08:55,460 --> 00:08:58,160
I kept thinking, just one more task.

201
00:08:58,160 --> 00:09:00,500
But then it got really late.

202
00:09:00,500 --> 00:09:02,660
That happens to me sometimes too.

203
00:09:02,660 --> 00:09:04,960
It's hard to stop when you're focused.

204
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:05,960
Exactly.

205
00:09:05,960 --> 00:09:09,760
But I guess I'll just grab some coffee and try to wake up.

206
00:09:09,760 --> 00:09:11,160
That sounds like a good plan.

207
00:09:11,160 --> 00:09:13,200
Coffee usually helps.

208
00:09:13,200 --> 00:09:14,920
So how was your weekend?

209
00:09:14,920 --> 00:09:16,320
It was great, actually.

210
00:09:16,320 --> 00:09:19,760
I spent time with my family and also did some reading.

211
00:09:19,760 --> 00:09:21,640
It was very relaxing.

212
00:09:21,640 --> 00:09:22,880
What about you?

213
00:09:22,880 --> 00:09:25,640
Mine was a mix of work and relaxation.

214
00:09:25,640 --> 00:09:30,180
On Saturday, I had to finish a report, but on Sunday, I went out with friends.

215
00:09:30,180 --> 00:09:31,720
That sounds like a good balance.

216
00:09:31,720 --> 00:09:33,280
Yeah, it was.

217
00:09:33,280 --> 00:09:36,800
I feel ready for the new week, even if I'm a bit tired.

218
00:09:36,800 --> 00:09:38,800
So what's on your plate today?

219
00:09:38,800 --> 00:09:41,280
I have quite a few things to do.

220
00:09:41,280 --> 00:09:46,920
I need to prepare for a meeting, respond to emails, and finish a client proposal.

221
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:47,920
That sounds like a lot.

222
00:09:47,920 --> 00:09:49,800
I'm also pretty busy today.

223
00:09:49,800 --> 00:09:51,760
I have deadlines coming up.

224
00:09:51,760 --> 00:09:53,880
Looks like we're both swamped.

225
00:09:53,880 --> 00:09:56,120
Definitely, but we'll manage.

226
00:09:56,120 --> 00:09:58,280
Hey, Sophia, do you have a minute?

227
00:09:58,280 --> 00:09:59,280
Sure, Daniel.

228
00:09:59,280 --> 00:10:00,280
What do you need?

229
00:10:00,280 --> 00:10:04,480
I'm working on this report, but I'm not sure if I'm using the correct format.

230
00:10:04,480 --> 00:10:05,960
Could you take a quick look?

231
00:10:05,960 --> 00:10:06,960
Of course.

232
00:10:06,960 --> 00:10:08,080
Let me see.

233
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:09,080
Here it is.

234
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:10,080
Hmm.

235
00:10:10,080 --> 00:10:14,560
Overall, it looks good, but I think you should add a summary at the beginning.

236
00:10:14,560 --> 00:10:16,280
Oh, that's a good idea.

237
00:10:16,280 --> 00:10:17,840
I didn't think about that.

238
00:10:17,840 --> 00:10:21,480
It helps readers understand the main points quickly.

239
00:10:21,480 --> 00:10:22,480
That makes sense.

240
00:10:22,480 --> 00:10:24,040
Thanks for your suggestion.

241
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:25,040
You're welcome.

242
00:10:25,040 --> 00:10:27,400
Daniel, can I ask you something?

243
00:10:27,400 --> 00:10:28,400
Of course.

244
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:31,280
I'm having trouble understanding this data.

245
00:10:31,280 --> 00:10:33,120
Could you explain it to me?

246
00:10:33,120 --> 00:10:34,120
Sure.

247
00:10:34,120 --> 00:10:36,280
This part shows the monthly growth rate.

248
00:10:36,280 --> 00:10:39,960
Oh, I see. And what about this section?

249
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:42,360
That's the comparison with last year.

250
00:10:42,360 --> 00:10:44,600
Got it. Thanks for explaining.

251
00:10:44,600 --> 00:10:49,080
No problem at all. Sorry to bother you again. Are you busy right now?

252
00:10:49,080 --> 00:10:54,120
I'm in the middle of something, but I can help you in about 10 minutes. Is that okay?

253
00:10:54,120 --> 00:10:57,000
Yes, that's perfectly fine. I'll come back later.

254
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:57,960
Great.

255
00:10:57,960 --> 00:10:59,880
Let's get started with the meeting.

256
00:10:59,880 --> 00:11:01,560
Good morning, everyone.

257
00:11:01,560 --> 00:11:03,320
Thank you all for being here.

258
00:11:03,320 --> 00:11:07,000
Today we're going to discuss the new project timeline.

259
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,080
Sophia, would you like to begin?

260
00:11:09,080 --> 00:11:12,760
Sure. I'll start by outlining the main goals.

261
00:11:12,760 --> 00:11:13,960
Sounds good.

262
00:11:13,960 --> 00:11:18,200
Our objective is to complete the project within three months.

263
00:11:18,200 --> 00:11:21,800
That seems reasonable. Excuse me, can I add something?

264
00:11:21,800 --> 00:11:22,920
Of course.

265
00:11:22,920 --> 00:11:25,960
I think we should also consider potential risks.

266
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:27,800
That's a great point.

267
00:11:27,800 --> 00:11:31,480
For example, delays in delivery could affect the timeline.

268
00:11:31,480 --> 00:11:33,800
I agree. We should plan for that.

269
00:11:33,800 --> 00:11:38,600
I understand your point, Sophia, but I think the deadline might be too tight.

270
00:11:38,600 --> 00:11:41,120
That's fair. What do you suggest?

271
00:11:41,120 --> 00:11:43,720
Maybe we can extend it by one week?

272
00:11:43,720 --> 00:11:46,720
That could work. What does everyone else think?

273
00:11:46,720 --> 00:11:48,520
I'm on board with that idea.

274
00:11:48,520 --> 00:11:50,440
Great. Let's go with that.

275
00:11:50,440 --> 00:11:52,400
Does anyone have any questions?

276
00:11:52,400 --> 00:11:54,120
No questions from me.

277
00:11:54,120 --> 00:11:55,880
Alright, let's wrap up.

278
00:11:55,880 --> 00:12:00,760
To summarize, we agreed on the timeline and discussed possible risks.

279
00:12:00,760 --> 00:12:02,080
Thank you everyone.

280
00:12:02,080 --> 00:12:03,400
Thanks for your time.

281
00:12:03,400 --> 00:12:05,040
That meeting went well.

282
00:12:05,040 --> 00:12:07,400
Yes, it was very productive.

283
00:12:07,400 --> 00:12:08,960
I liked your ideas.

284
00:12:08,960 --> 00:12:10,960
Thank you, I appreciate that.

285
00:12:10,960 --> 00:12:12,840
Hey, are you going for lunch?

286
00:12:12,840 --> 00:12:15,320
Yes, I am. Do you want to join me?

287
00:12:15,320 --> 00:12:16,920
Sure, I'd love to.

288
00:12:16,920 --> 00:12:18,840
Great, where should we go?

289
00:12:18,840 --> 00:12:21,040
Maybe the cafe nearby?

290
00:12:21,040 --> 00:12:22,160
Sounds good.

291
00:12:22,160 --> 00:12:24,440
So how's your project going?

292
00:12:24,440 --> 00:12:27,160
It's going well, but it's quite challenging.

293
00:12:27,160 --> 00:12:29,240
What's the most difficult part?

294
00:12:29,240 --> 00:12:31,240
Managing the timeline.

295
00:12:31,240 --> 00:12:34,240
I understand. Deadlines can be stressful.

296
00:12:34,240 --> 00:12:37,240
Yes, but I'm learning a lot.

297
00:12:37,240 --> 00:12:42,240
That's good. By the way, that presentation you gave earlier was excellent.

298
00:12:42,240 --> 00:12:43,240
Thank you so much.

299
00:12:43,240 --> 00:12:46,240
You explained everything very clearly.

300
00:12:46,240 --> 00:12:47,240
I'm glad you think so.

301
00:12:47,240 --> 00:12:49,240
You did a great job.

302
00:12:49,240 --> 00:12:51,240
I appreciate it.

303
00:12:51,240 --> 00:12:54,240
I'm sorry for the delay in replying to your email.

304
00:12:54,240 --> 00:12:55,240
That's okay.

305
00:12:55,240 --> 00:12:57,240
I had a lot of work yesterday.

306
00:12:57,240 --> 00:12:59,240
No worries, I understand.

307
00:12:59,240 --> 00:13:02,240
Are you free later to discuss the project?

308
00:13:02,240 --> 00:13:05,240
I have a meeting at three, but I'm free after that.

309
00:13:05,240 --> 00:13:07,240
Perfect. Let's meet at four.

310
00:13:07,240 --> 00:13:08,240
Sounds good.

311
00:13:08,240 --> 00:13:11,240
Let's touch base later about the client feedback.

312
00:13:11,240 --> 00:13:12,240
Sure.

313
00:13:12,240 --> 00:13:15,240
And please keep me posted if there are any updates.

314
00:13:15,240 --> 00:13:16,240
I will.

315
00:13:16,240 --> 00:13:18,240
Do you want to grab a coffee?

316
00:13:18,240 --> 00:13:20,240
Yes, I need a break.

317
00:13:20,240 --> 00:13:21,240
Let's go.

318
00:13:21,240 --> 00:13:22,240
Great.

319
00:13:22,240 --> 00:13:25,240
A few of us are going out after work. Do you want to come?

320
00:13:25,240 --> 00:13:32,040
to come? I'd love to, but I already have plans. No problem. Maybe next time. I'm heading

321
00:13:32,040 --> 00:13:38,680
out now. Okay, have a great evening. You too. See you tomorrow. See ya. It's Friday. Any

322
00:13:38,680 --> 00:13:45,080
plans for the weekend? Yes, I'm going hiking. That sounds fun. What about you? I'm just

323
00:13:45,080 --> 00:13:51,520
going to relax. That's nice too. Have a great weekend. You too. Hey, Sophia, just

324
00:13:51,520 --> 00:13:54,040
following up on our earlier discussion.

325
00:13:54,040 --> 00:13:55,040
Yes.

326
00:13:55,040 --> 00:13:56,920
Did you complete the report?

327
00:13:56,920 --> 00:13:57,720
Almost.

328
00:13:57,720 --> 00:13:59,080
I'll finish it today.

329
00:13:59,080 --> 00:13:59,920
Great.

330
00:13:59,920 --> 00:14:02,120
Can you swing by my desk later?

331
00:14:02,120 --> 00:14:03,000
Sure.

332
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:03,960
Thanks.

333
00:14:03,960 --> 00:14:05,080
No problem.

334
00:14:05,080 --> 00:14:06,960
Let's catch up next week.

335
00:14:06,960 --> 00:14:08,120
I'd like that.

336
00:14:08,120 --> 00:14:09,720
Maybe over lunch?

337
00:14:09,720 --> 00:14:11,080
Sounds perfect.

338
00:14:11,080 --> 00:14:13,080
Today was a busy day.

339
00:14:13,080 --> 00:14:15,680
Yes, but we accomplished a lot.

340
00:14:15,680 --> 00:14:16,840
That's true.

341
00:14:16,840 --> 00:14:18,160
Good teamwork.

342
00:14:18,160 --> 00:14:19,440
Absolutely.

343
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:22,720
Talking with coworkers becomes easier with practice.

344
00:14:22,720 --> 00:14:26,160
Yes. The more you practice, the more natural it feels.

345
00:14:26,160 --> 00:14:28,840
And remember to be polite and friendly.

346
00:14:28,840 --> 00:14:30,760
That's the most important thing.

347
00:14:30,760 --> 00:14:32,280
Thanks for joining us.

348
00:14:32,280 --> 00:14:34,280
Keep practicing every day.

349
00:14:34,280 --> 00:14:35,720
See you next time.

350
00:14:35,720 --> 00:14:36,680
Goodbye.

351
00:14:36,680 --> 00:14:39,240
Welcome back to Business English Learning.

352
00:14:39,240 --> 00:14:40,160
Hi, everyone.

353
00:14:40,160 --> 00:14:43,320
Welcome to today's English Conversation Practice.

354
00:14:43,320 --> 00:14:46,480
I'm Daniel, and I'm really excited about today's episode

355
00:14:46,480 --> 00:14:50,560
because this is something you will use every single day at work.

356
00:14:50,560 --> 00:14:51,560
And I'm Sophia.

357
00:14:51,560 --> 00:14:54,200
We're so happy you're here with us.

358
00:14:54,200 --> 00:14:58,360
Today's topic is how to talk with coworkers in English, and we're going to make this

359
00:14:58,360 --> 00:15:05,200
very practical, very natural, and very comprehensive so you can actually use these conversations

360
00:15:05,200 --> 00:15:06,600
in real life.

361
00:15:06,600 --> 00:15:07,600
Exactly.

362
00:15:07,600 --> 00:15:11,600
We're not just going to give you phrases, we're going to show you real conversations

363
00:15:11,600 --> 00:15:14,360
from morning to evening in a workplace.

364
00:15:14,360 --> 00:15:18,000
Yes, imagine you are going through a full work day.

365
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:24,600
You arrive at the office, talk to co-workers, ask for help, attend meetings, have lunch,

366
00:15:24,600 --> 00:15:27,680
deal with problems, and then leave for the day.

367
00:15:27,680 --> 00:15:29,120
Let's start with the morning.

368
00:15:29,120 --> 00:15:33,560
You walk into the office and see your co-worker for the first time that day.

369
00:15:33,560 --> 00:15:34,720
What do you say?

370
00:15:34,720 --> 00:15:39,720
You can say, good morning, which is the safest and most professional option.

371
00:15:39,720 --> 00:15:45,720
If your office is more relaxed, you can say morning or even hey, good morning. Let's act it out

372
00:15:46,120 --> 00:15:53,080
Good morning, Sophia. How are you today? Good morning, Daniel? I'm doing well. Thanks. I feel pretty energized today

373
00:15:53,080 --> 00:15:59,800
How about you? I'm doing okay. I'm still waking up to be honest. I need my coffee. That's very natural

374
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:03,680
You don't need perfect sentences. Just speak simply and honestly

375
00:16:03,680 --> 00:16:04,680
Honestly.

376
00:16:04,680 --> 00:16:08,120
After greetings, we usually move into small talk.

377
00:16:08,120 --> 00:16:10,520
This is where many learners feel uncomfortable.

378
00:16:10,520 --> 00:16:16,320
Yes, but small talk is actually easy if you remember a few safe topics.

379
00:16:16,320 --> 00:16:17,640
Let's try one.

380
00:16:17,640 --> 00:16:19,520
Daniel, how was your weekend?

381
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:20,880
It was really nice.

382
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:23,680
I went out with some friends and tried a new restaurant.

383
00:16:23,680 --> 00:16:24,680
What about you?

384
00:16:24,680 --> 00:16:25,680
That sounds fun.

385
00:16:25,680 --> 00:16:27,040
I had a quiet weekend.

386
00:16:27,040 --> 00:16:30,720
I stayed home, watched a series and did some cleaning.

387
00:16:30,720 --> 00:16:32,360
That's perfect small talk.

388
00:16:32,360 --> 00:16:34,500
short, simple, and friendly.

389
00:16:34,500 --> 00:16:37,380
You can also talk about the weather, for example,

390
00:16:37,380 --> 00:16:42,380
it's really cold today or such a nice, sunny morning.

391
00:16:42,620 --> 00:16:45,680
Or even traffic was terrible this morning.

392
00:16:45,680 --> 00:16:46,940
That's also common.

393
00:16:46,940 --> 00:16:49,300
Yes, especially in big cities.

394
00:16:49,300 --> 00:16:53,300
Now let's move to a slightly more work-related situation.

395
00:16:53,300 --> 00:16:54,660
You arrive at your desk

396
00:16:54,660 --> 00:16:56,860
and you need to ask a co-worker something.

397
00:16:56,860 --> 00:16:57,940
How do you start?

398
00:16:57,940 --> 00:16:59,460
Always start politely.

399
00:16:59,460 --> 00:17:02,700
For example, excuse me, do you have a minute?

400
00:17:02,700 --> 00:17:04,060
Let's try that.

401
00:17:04,060 --> 00:17:05,980
Hey Sophia, do you have a minute?

402
00:17:05,980 --> 00:17:07,660
Sure, what can I help you with?

403
00:17:07,660 --> 00:17:09,340
I'm working on the sales report,

404
00:17:09,340 --> 00:17:11,300
but I'm not sure about this data.

405
00:17:11,300 --> 00:17:12,540
Could you take a look?

406
00:17:12,540 --> 00:17:14,660
Of course, let me see.

407
00:17:14,660 --> 00:17:17,940
Oh, I think this number needs to be updated.

408
00:17:17,940 --> 00:17:19,260
Ah, I see.

409
00:17:19,260 --> 00:17:21,100
Thanks a lot, that really helps.

410
00:17:21,100 --> 00:17:22,780
You're welcome, anytime.

411
00:17:22,780 --> 00:17:24,660
That's a perfect example.

412
00:17:24,660 --> 00:17:27,940
Notice how polite and simple the conversation is.

413
00:17:27,940 --> 00:17:30,860
Now what if the co-worker is busy?

414
00:17:30,860 --> 00:17:31,820
Good question.

415
00:17:31,820 --> 00:17:32,820
Let's try it.

416
00:17:32,820 --> 00:17:34,700
Hey, Sophia, do you have a minute?

417
00:17:34,700 --> 00:17:36,620
I'm a bit tied up right now.

418
00:17:36,620 --> 00:17:38,700
Can we talk in about 20 minutes?

419
00:17:38,700 --> 00:17:39,820
Sure, no problem.

420
00:17:39,820 --> 00:17:41,260
Just let me know when you're free.

421
00:17:41,260 --> 00:17:45,180
That's how you handle it politely without any awkwardness.

422
00:17:45,180 --> 00:17:47,540
Now let's move to collaboration.

423
00:17:47,540 --> 00:17:50,300
Imagine you are working on a project together.

424
00:17:50,300 --> 00:17:53,980
Yes, teamwork conversations are very important.

425
00:17:53,980 --> 00:17:57,340
Sophia, have you had a chance to review the presentation?

426
00:17:57,340 --> 00:18:02,140
Yes, I looked at it this morning. It's really good, but I think we should add more data to

427
00:18:02,140 --> 00:18:06,700
support our points. That's a good idea. I can work on that this afternoon.

428
00:18:06,700 --> 00:18:10,220
Great. Let me know if you need any help. I will. Thanks.

429
00:18:10,220 --> 00:18:13,820
Notice how we give feedback politely. We don't say,

430
00:18:13,820 --> 00:18:17,900
this is bad. We say, it's good, but we can improve it.

431
00:18:17,900 --> 00:18:21,180
That's very important in workplace communication.

432
00:18:21,180 --> 00:18:26,540
Now let's talk about meetings. Meetings can be stressful if you don't know what to say.

433
00:18:26,540 --> 00:18:29,140
True. Let's imagine we're in a meeting.

434
00:18:29,140 --> 00:18:29,940
Okay.

435
00:18:29,940 --> 00:18:33,940
I'd like to start by saying that our sales have improved this quarter.

436
00:18:33,940 --> 00:18:36,740
That's great news! Can I add something?

437
00:18:36,740 --> 00:18:37,540
Of course.

438
00:18:37,540 --> 00:18:42,440
I think we should also look at customer feedback to understand what's working well.

439
00:18:42,440 --> 00:18:43,740
That's a great point.

440
00:18:43,740 --> 00:18:46,940
Now let's try disagreeing politely.

441
00:18:46,940 --> 00:18:50,640
Okay. I think we should launch the product next week.

442
00:18:50,640 --> 00:18:55,040
I see your point, but I think we might need more time for testing.

443
00:18:55,040 --> 00:18:56,140
That's reasonable.

444
00:18:56,140 --> 00:18:58,140
Maybe we can delay it by a week.

445
00:18:58,140 --> 00:19:00,140
That sounds like a good compromise.

446
00:19:00,140 --> 00:19:03,140
See how we disagree without being rude?

447
00:19:03,140 --> 00:19:05,140
Yes, that's a key skill.

448
00:19:05,140 --> 00:19:08,140
Now let's move to a more casual situation.

449
00:19:08,140 --> 00:19:09,140
Lunchtime.

450
00:19:09,140 --> 00:19:11,140
This is where you can build friendships.

451
00:19:11,140 --> 00:19:14,140
Hey Sophia, are you free for lunch?

452
00:19:14,140 --> 00:19:17,140
Yes, I am. Do you want to go out or eat here?

453
00:19:17,140 --> 00:19:20,140
Let's go out. I feel like getting something different today.

454
00:19:20,140 --> 00:19:23,140
Sounds good. There's a new cafe nearby. Want to try it?

455
00:19:23,140 --> 00:19:25,140
Sure, let's do that.

456
00:19:25,140 --> 00:19:28,220
That's how you make simple plans with co-workers.

457
00:19:28,220 --> 00:19:31,180
Now what if someone invites you but you're busy?

458
00:19:31,180 --> 00:19:32,260
Let's try.

459
00:19:32,260 --> 00:19:34,420
Hey Sophia, do you want to grab lunch?

460
00:19:34,420 --> 00:19:38,140
I'd love to, but I have a deadline today, maybe another time.

461
00:19:38,140 --> 00:19:39,860
No problem, maybe tomorrow.

462
00:19:39,860 --> 00:19:42,140
Perfect, polite and friendly.

463
00:19:42,140 --> 00:19:46,460
Now let's talk about handling a small problem or misunderstanding.

464
00:19:46,460 --> 00:19:48,580
This is very realistic.

465
00:19:48,580 --> 00:19:51,660
Sophia, I noticed the file was changed.

466
00:19:51,660 --> 00:19:52,820
Did you update it?

467
00:19:52,820 --> 00:19:56,420
Yes, I made a few edits this morning. Was there an issue?

468
00:19:56,420 --> 00:20:00,180
I think some of the data might have been removed by mistake.

469
00:20:00,180 --> 00:20:03,860
Oh, I'm sorry about that. Let me check and fix it.

470
00:20:03,860 --> 00:20:06,020
No worries. Thanks for looking into it.

471
00:20:06,020 --> 00:20:10,020
This is a great example of staying calm and professional.

472
00:20:10,020 --> 00:20:12,660
Now let's talk about giving compliments.

473
00:20:12,660 --> 00:20:15,940
Yes, very important for good relationships.

474
00:20:15,940 --> 00:20:21,300
Sophia, great job on the presentation today. You explained everything very clearly.

475
00:20:21,300 --> 00:20:24,020
Thank you, Daniel. I really appreciate that.

476
00:20:24,020 --> 00:20:26,580
You deserve it. It was excellent work.

477
00:20:26,580 --> 00:20:28,580
Thank you. That means a lot.

478
00:20:28,580 --> 00:20:31,380
Simple, positive, and encouraging.

479
00:20:31,380 --> 00:20:34,260
Now let's talk about the end of the day.

480
00:20:34,260 --> 00:20:36,980
Yes. You're about to leave the office.

481
00:20:36,980 --> 00:20:39,540
You can say, I'm heading out now.

482
00:20:39,540 --> 00:20:41,380
Or, see you tomorrow.

483
00:20:41,380 --> 00:20:42,500
Let's try it.

484
00:20:42,500 --> 00:20:45,540
All right. I'm heading out. See you tomorrow, Sophia.

485
00:20:45,540 --> 00:20:48,100
See you tomorrow, Daniel. Have a great evening.

486
00:20:48,100 --> 00:20:49,540
You too. Take care.

487
00:20:49,540 --> 00:20:52,980
And on Friday you can say, have a great weekend!

488
00:20:52,980 --> 00:20:54,100
Exactly!

489
00:20:54,100 --> 00:20:59,940
Before we finish, let's have a longer natural conversation combining everything.

490
00:20:59,940 --> 00:21:00,980
Great idea!

491
00:21:00,980 --> 00:21:03,860
Good morning, Daniel. How's everything going today?

492
00:21:03,860 --> 00:21:06,100
Good morning, Sophia. It's going well.

493
00:21:06,100 --> 00:21:10,020
I have quite a bit on my plate, but I'm managing. How about you?

494
00:21:10,020 --> 00:21:13,140
Same here. It's a busy day, but I'm making progress.

495
00:21:13,140 --> 00:21:14,900
Did you finish the report?

496
00:21:14,900 --> 00:21:18,500
Almost. I just need to review a few details.

497
00:21:18,500 --> 00:21:20,180
Could you take a quick look later?

498
00:21:20,180 --> 00:21:23,540
Sure, I'd be happy to. Just send it to me when you're ready.

499
00:21:23,540 --> 00:21:25,180
Thanks, I appreciate it.

500
00:21:25,180 --> 00:21:28,220
By the way, are you joining the meeting this afternoon?

501
00:21:28,220 --> 00:21:31,580
Yes, I am. I think it's going to be an important one.

502
00:21:31,580 --> 00:21:35,980
Definitely. I want to share an idea about improving our workflow.

503
00:21:35,980 --> 00:21:38,460
That sounds interesting. I'd love to hear it.

504
00:21:38,460 --> 00:21:41,540
Maybe we can discuss it briefly before the meeting.

505
00:21:41,540 --> 00:21:44,300
Good idea. Let's catch up after lunch.

506
00:21:44,300 --> 00:21:46,820
Speaking of lunch, are you free today?

507
00:21:46,820 --> 00:21:49,540
Yes, I am. Do you want to grab something together?

508
00:21:49,540 --> 00:21:51,020
Sure, that would be great.

509
00:21:51,020 --> 00:21:53,420
Perfect. Let's go around 12.30.

510
00:21:53,420 --> 00:21:58,180
Sounds good. Oh, and by the way, great job on yesterday's presentation.

511
00:21:58,180 --> 00:22:00,820
Thank you so much. I really appreciate that.

512
00:22:00,820 --> 00:22:03,380
No problem. It was really impressive.

513
00:22:03,380 --> 00:22:05,580
Thanks, Daniel. That means a lot.

514
00:22:05,580 --> 00:22:08,980
Alright. I'll finish my work and send you the report soon.

515
00:22:08,980 --> 00:22:11,100
Great. I'll keep an eye out for it.

516
00:22:11,100 --> 00:22:11,980
Thanks again.

517
00:22:11,980 --> 00:22:13,180
Any time.

518
00:22:13,180 --> 00:22:17,180
This has been such a comprehensive and practical conversation.

519
00:22:17,180 --> 00:22:22,980
Yes, and remember, the goal is not perfection, the goal is communication.

520
00:22:22,980 --> 00:22:26,180
Be polite, be friendly, and be confident.

521
00:22:26,180 --> 00:22:30,580
Practice these conversations every day and you will improve quickly.

522
00:22:30,580 --> 00:22:32,480
Thank you so much for listening.

523
00:22:32,480 --> 00:22:34,180
See you in the next episode.

524
00:22:34,180 --> 00:22:35,380
Goodbye, everyone.

525
00:22:35,380 --> 00:22:36,180
Bye.

526
00:22:36,180 --> 00:22:38,680
Welcome back to Business English Learning.

527
00:22:38,680 --> 00:22:39,780
Hi, everyone.

528
00:22:39,780 --> 00:22:42,880
Welcome to today's English conversation practice.

529
00:22:42,880 --> 00:22:43,880
I'm Daniel.

530
00:22:43,880 --> 00:22:48,760
And I'm Sophia, and we are here to help you speak English naturally and confidently

531
00:22:48,760 --> 00:22:50,840
in real-life situations.

532
00:22:50,840 --> 00:22:54,600
Today we have a very practical and useful topic for you.

533
00:22:54,600 --> 00:22:57,160
How to talk with co-workers in English.

534
00:22:57,160 --> 00:23:01,540
Yes, this is something you will use every single day if you work in an office or any

535
00:23:01,540 --> 00:23:03,320
professional environment.

536
00:23:03,320 --> 00:23:05,800
At work, you don't just speak English.

537
00:23:05,800 --> 00:23:09,760
You communicate, build relationships, and work as a team.

538
00:23:09,760 --> 00:23:10,760
Exactly.

539
00:23:10,760 --> 00:23:13,200
Sometimes the hardest part is not grammar.

540
00:23:13,200 --> 00:23:16,160
It's knowing what to say in real situations.

541
00:23:16,160 --> 00:23:21,320
So today we'll show you natural conversations you can use at work right away.

542
00:23:21,320 --> 00:23:23,960
Let's start with a very common situation.

543
00:23:23,960 --> 00:23:25,800
Arriving at the office in the morning.

544
00:23:25,800 --> 00:23:26,800
Good morning.

545
00:23:26,800 --> 00:23:27,800
How are you today?

546
00:23:27,800 --> 00:23:28,800
Good morning.

547
00:23:28,800 --> 00:23:29,800
I'm doing well.

548
00:23:29,800 --> 00:23:30,800
Thanks.

549
00:23:30,800 --> 00:23:31,800
How about you?

550
00:23:31,800 --> 00:23:32,800
I'm good.

551
00:23:32,800 --> 00:23:33,800
Just a bit sleepy today.

552
00:23:33,800 --> 00:23:34,800
I didn't sleep enough last night.

553
00:23:34,800 --> 00:23:35,800
Oh no, that happens.

554
00:23:35,800 --> 00:23:37,720
Maybe you need an extra coffee.

555
00:23:37,720 --> 00:23:38,720
Definitely.

556
00:23:38,720 --> 00:23:41,400
I think I'll grab one right after I sit down.

557
00:23:41,400 --> 00:23:42,400
Same here.

558
00:23:42,400 --> 00:23:44,200
So, how was your evening yesterday?

559
00:23:44,200 --> 00:23:45,360
It was pretty relaxing.

560
00:23:45,360 --> 00:23:47,520
I stayed home and watched a series.

561
00:23:47,520 --> 00:23:48,520
How about you?

562
00:23:48,520 --> 00:23:49,800
I had a busy evening.

563
00:23:49,800 --> 00:23:52,840
I finished some work and replied to emails.

564
00:23:52,840 --> 00:23:53,840
Sounds productive?

565
00:23:53,840 --> 00:23:56,640
Yeah, a little too productive actually.

566
00:23:56,640 --> 00:23:59,800
By the way, did you see the message about the team meeting today?

567
00:23:59,800 --> 00:24:00,800
Yes, I did.

568
00:24:00,800 --> 00:24:02,440
It's at 10.30, right?

569
00:24:02,440 --> 00:24:03,440
That's right.

570
00:24:03,440 --> 00:24:04,440
Are you ready for it?

571
00:24:04,440 --> 00:24:05,440
Almost.

572
00:24:05,440 --> 00:24:07,240
I still need to review my notes.

573
00:24:07,240 --> 00:24:08,240
Same here.

574
00:24:08,240 --> 00:24:10,680
Go through it before the meeting if we have time.

575
00:24:10,680 --> 00:24:11,680
Good idea.

576
00:24:11,680 --> 00:24:12,680
Hey, excuse me.

577
00:24:12,680 --> 00:24:13,680
Do you have a minute?

578
00:24:13,680 --> 00:24:14,680
Sure.

579
00:24:14,680 --> 00:24:15,680
What's up?

580
00:24:15,680 --> 00:24:18,480
I'm working on this report and I'm a bit confused about one part.

581
00:24:18,480 --> 00:24:19,480
Could you help me?

582
00:24:19,480 --> 00:24:20,480
Of course.

583
00:24:20,480 --> 00:24:21,480
Let me take a look.

584
00:24:21,480 --> 00:24:22,480
Thanks.

585
00:24:22,480 --> 00:24:23,480
I really appreciate it.

586
00:24:23,480 --> 00:24:24,480
No problem.

587
00:24:24,480 --> 00:24:28,520
Okay, I think this section needs more explanation and a clear example.

588
00:24:28,520 --> 00:24:29,760
Oh, I see.

589
00:24:29,760 --> 00:24:30,960
That makes sense.

590
00:24:30,960 --> 00:24:33,520
And maybe add a short summary at the end.

591
00:24:33,520 --> 00:24:35,400
That's a great suggestion.

592
00:24:35,400 --> 00:24:36,400
You're welcome.

593
00:24:36,400 --> 00:24:38,520
By the way, are you free for lunch today?

594
00:24:38,520 --> 00:24:39,520
I think so.

595
00:24:39,520 --> 00:24:40,920
Do you want to grab something together?

596
00:24:40,920 --> 00:24:42,560
Yes, that would be nice.

597
00:24:42,560 --> 00:24:43,560
Great.

598
00:24:43,560 --> 00:24:44,560
Where should we go?

599
00:24:44,560 --> 00:24:46,360
There's a new cafe near the office.

600
00:24:46,360 --> 00:24:47,360
Have you tried it?

601
00:24:47,360 --> 00:24:49,560
Not yet, but I've heard good things about it.

602
00:24:49,560 --> 00:24:50,560
Perfect.

603
00:24:50,560 --> 00:24:51,560
Let's try it then.

604
00:24:51,560 --> 00:24:52,560
Sounds good.

605
00:24:52,560 --> 00:24:54,640
Hey, I have a quick question for you.

606
00:24:54,640 --> 00:24:55,640
Sure.

607
00:24:55,640 --> 00:24:57,360
Are you going to the meeting this afternoon?

608
00:24:57,360 --> 00:24:58,360
Yes, I am.

609
00:24:58,360 --> 00:24:59,360
Why?

610
00:24:59,360 --> 00:25:02,080
I'm a bit nervous about speaking in the meeting.

611
00:25:02,080 --> 00:25:03,080
Don't worry.

612
00:25:03,080 --> 00:25:04,640
Just keep it simple and clear.

613
00:25:04,640 --> 00:25:06,280
That's easier said than done.

614
00:25:06,280 --> 00:25:09,280
True, but you can prepare a few key points.

615
00:25:09,280 --> 00:25:11,280
Good idea. Maybe I should practice.

616
00:25:11,280 --> 00:25:13,280
Yes, I can help you if you want.

617
00:25:13,280 --> 00:25:15,280
That would be really helpful.

618
00:25:15,280 --> 00:25:18,280
Okay, let's try. What do you want to say?

619
00:25:18,280 --> 00:25:22,280
Maybe something like, excuse me, I'd like to share an update.

620
00:25:22,280 --> 00:25:24,280
Perfect. That sounds very professional.

621
00:25:24,280 --> 00:25:27,280
And then I explain my idea, right?

622
00:25:27,280 --> 00:25:30,280
Exactly. Just speak slowly and confidently.

623
00:25:30,280 --> 00:25:32,280
What if someone disagrees with me?

624
00:25:32,280 --> 00:25:38,760
You can say I understand your point, but I think that keeps it polite. That sounds really useful

625
00:25:38,760 --> 00:25:41,760
It is politeness is very important at work

626
00:25:42,520 --> 00:25:50,520
Definitely, okay, let's continue with another situation working on a project deadline. Oh, yes deadlines can be stressful

627
00:25:50,760 --> 00:25:57,240
Hey, I just got an email from the manager. What does it say the report needs to be finished by tomorrow morning?

628
00:25:57,400 --> 00:26:01,840
Wow, that's urgent. Yes a bit stressful. Are you okay with that?

629
00:26:01,840 --> 00:26:04,840
I think so, but I may need some help.

630
00:26:04,840 --> 00:26:06,840
Sure, we can work on it together.

631
00:26:06,840 --> 00:26:08,840
Thanks, I really appreciate it.

632
00:26:08,840 --> 00:26:10,840
No problem. Teamwork makes it easier.

633
00:26:10,840 --> 00:26:12,840
Absolutely.

634
00:26:12,840 --> 00:26:15,840
Hey, how do you usually write emails to coworkers?

635
00:26:15,840 --> 00:26:19,840
I keep it simple. I start with hi or hello in their name.

636
00:26:19,840 --> 00:26:20,840
Same here.

637
00:26:20,840 --> 00:26:23,840
Then I clearly explain what I need or what I'm updating.

638
00:26:23,840 --> 00:26:26,840
And I always try to be polite and direct.

639
00:26:26,840 --> 00:26:30,840
Yes, and I end with thanks or best regards.

640
00:26:30,840 --> 00:26:32,080
That's a good habit.

641
00:26:32,080 --> 00:26:35,200
Okay, let's imagine we are in the office kitchen.

642
00:26:35,200 --> 00:26:37,760
That's where the best small talk happens.

643
00:26:37,760 --> 00:26:39,080
Hey, that looks good.

644
00:26:39,080 --> 00:26:40,120
What are you having?

645
00:26:40,120 --> 00:26:42,040
I brought lunch from home today.

646
00:26:42,040 --> 00:26:43,880
Nice, it smells great.

647
00:26:43,880 --> 00:26:45,560
Thanks, what about you?

648
00:26:45,560 --> 00:26:47,160
I'm planning to order something.

649
00:26:47,160 --> 00:26:48,440
Any suggestions?

650
00:26:48,440 --> 00:26:49,760
There's a good place nearby

651
00:26:49,760 --> 00:26:51,920
that serves really good noodles.

652
00:26:51,920 --> 00:26:53,960
Sounds perfect, I'll try that.

653
00:26:53,960 --> 00:26:54,920
Good choice.

654
00:26:54,920 --> 00:26:56,640
Hey, do you need a hand with that?

655
00:26:56,640 --> 00:26:58,520
Yes, please, that would be great.

656
00:26:58,520 --> 00:26:59,560
No problem.

657
00:26:59,560 --> 00:27:00,760
Thanks for your help.

658
00:27:00,760 --> 00:27:01,840
Any time.

659
00:27:01,840 --> 00:27:04,400
Now let's move to the end of the workday.

660
00:27:04,400 --> 00:27:07,320
Yes, saying goodbye is also important.

661
00:27:07,320 --> 00:27:08,560
I'm heading out now.

662
00:27:08,560 --> 00:27:10,040
Okay, have a good evening.

663
00:27:10,040 --> 00:27:11,320
Thanks, you too.

664
00:27:11,320 --> 00:27:12,280
See you tomorrow.

665
00:27:12,280 --> 00:27:13,120
See you.

666
00:27:13,120 --> 00:27:15,840
And if it's Friday, we can say something special.

667
00:27:15,840 --> 00:27:17,960
Right, have a great weekend.

668
00:27:17,960 --> 00:27:19,080
Exactly.

669
00:27:19,080 --> 00:27:21,880
And on Monday, we ask, how was your weekend?

670
00:27:21,880 --> 00:27:24,160
It's a simple but natural cycle.

671
00:27:24,160 --> 00:27:26,280
Before we finish, remember this.

672
00:27:26,280 --> 00:27:28,840
Communication at work is about being polite,

673
00:27:28,840 --> 00:27:30,400
clear, and friendly.

674
00:27:30,400 --> 00:27:33,000
Yes, don't worry about perfect English.

675
00:27:33,000 --> 00:27:34,740
Focus on connection.

676
00:27:34,740 --> 00:27:35,880
Mistakes are okay.

677
00:27:35,880 --> 00:27:37,960
What matters is communication.

678
00:27:37,960 --> 00:27:39,080
Absolutely.

679
00:27:39,080 --> 00:27:41,600
Keep practicing these phrases every day.

680
00:27:41,600 --> 00:27:44,400
And use them with your coworkers in real life.

681
00:27:44,400 --> 00:27:45,920
Thanks for listening, everyone.

682
00:27:45,920 --> 00:27:47,800
We'll see you in the next lesson.

683
00:27:47,800 --> 00:27:48,640
Goodbye.

684
00:27:48,640 --> 00:27:49,680
Bye, everyone.

685
00:27:49,680 --> 00:27:52,560
Welcome back to Business English Learning.

686
00:27:52,560 --> 00:27:53,400
Hi, everyone.

687
00:27:53,400 --> 00:27:56,760
Welcome to today's English Conversation Practice.

688
00:27:56,760 --> 00:27:57,840
I'm Daniel.

689
00:27:57,840 --> 00:27:59,000
And I'm Sophia.

690
00:27:59,000 --> 00:28:03,440
And we are here to help you speak English naturally and confidently at work.

691
00:28:03,440 --> 00:28:08,080
Today's topic is extremely practical and very important.

692
00:28:08,080 --> 00:28:13,880
We're going to show you how to talk with coworkers in English through real life conversations.

693
00:28:13,880 --> 00:28:14,760
That's right.

694
00:28:14,760 --> 00:28:20,560
Not just phrases, but full conversations you can imagine yourself having every day in the workplace.

695
00:28:20,560 --> 00:28:21,720
Exactly.

696
00:28:21,720 --> 00:28:26,840
From morning greetings to meetings, from asking for help to casual chats,

697
00:28:26,840 --> 00:28:30,320
We're going to walk through everything step by step.

698
00:28:30,320 --> 00:28:33,000
And remember, the goal is not perfection.

699
00:28:33,000 --> 00:28:35,880
The goal is communication, clear, polite,

700
00:28:35,880 --> 00:28:37,800
and natural communication.

701
00:28:37,800 --> 00:28:41,640
So let's begin with a typical morning at the office.

702
00:28:41,640 --> 00:28:42,680
Good morning, Zofia.

703
00:28:42,680 --> 00:28:43,920
How are you today?

704
00:28:43,920 --> 00:28:45,200
Good morning, Daniel.

705
00:28:45,200 --> 00:28:45,960
I'm doing well.

706
00:28:45,960 --> 00:28:46,840
Thank you.

707
00:28:46,840 --> 00:28:49,960
I slept early last night, so I feel refreshed.

708
00:28:49,960 --> 00:28:50,960
How about you?

709
00:28:50,960 --> 00:28:52,080
I'm doing OK.

710
00:28:52,080 --> 00:28:54,040
A bit sleepy, to be honest.

711
00:28:54,040 --> 00:28:56,560
I had a late dinner and didn't get enough rest.

712
00:28:56,560 --> 00:29:00,880
And that happens sometimes, hopefully a cup of coffee will fix that.

713
00:29:00,880 --> 00:29:01,880
Definitely.

714
00:29:01,880 --> 00:29:04,440
I already had one, but I might need another.

715
00:29:04,440 --> 00:29:06,560
So how was your commute this morning?

716
00:29:06,560 --> 00:29:08,040
It was smooth today.

717
00:29:08,040 --> 00:29:10,520
No traffic at all, which is rare.

718
00:29:10,520 --> 00:29:11,520
What about you?

719
00:29:11,520 --> 00:29:13,120
Mine was a bit slow.

720
00:29:13,120 --> 00:29:16,760
There was construction on the main road, so it took longer than usual.

721
00:29:16,760 --> 00:29:17,960
That's frustrating.

722
00:29:17,960 --> 00:29:19,800
At least you made it on time.

723
00:29:19,800 --> 00:29:21,480
Yes, thankfully.

724
00:29:21,480 --> 00:29:23,440
So do you have a busy day ahead?

725
00:29:23,440 --> 00:29:24,440
Yes, I do.

726
00:29:24,440 --> 00:29:29,200
I have two meetings and I need to finish a report by the end of the day.

727
00:29:29,200 --> 00:29:30,680
Sounds like a packed schedule.

728
00:29:30,680 --> 00:29:32,640
I also have a lot on my plate today.

729
00:29:32,640 --> 00:29:35,360
Well, let's stay focused and get through it.

730
00:29:35,360 --> 00:29:37,600
Hey, Sophia, do you have a minute?

731
00:29:37,600 --> 00:29:38,600
Sure, Daniel.

732
00:29:38,600 --> 00:29:39,600
What's up?

733
00:29:39,600 --> 00:29:43,640
I'm working on the sales report, but I'm a bit confused about the data from last

734
00:29:43,640 --> 00:29:44,640
quarter.

735
00:29:44,640 --> 00:29:46,200
Could you help me understand it?

736
00:29:46,200 --> 00:29:47,200
Of course.

737
00:29:47,200 --> 00:29:48,520
Let me take a look.

738
00:29:48,520 --> 00:29:50,600
Which part is confusing?

739
00:29:50,600 --> 00:29:51,600
This section here.

740
00:29:51,600 --> 00:29:54,200
I'm not sure how these numbers were calculated.

741
00:29:54,200 --> 00:30:02,200
Oh, I see. These numbers include both online and offline sales combined. That's why they look higher.

742
00:30:02,200 --> 00:30:06,200
Ah, that makes sense now. I was only looking at online sales.

743
00:30:06,200 --> 00:30:08,200
It's an easy mistake to make, don't worry.

744
00:30:08,200 --> 00:30:11,200
Thanks a lot for your help. I really appreciate it.

745
00:30:11,200 --> 00:30:14,200
No problem at all. Let me know if you need anything else.

746
00:30:14,200 --> 00:30:18,200
Sophia, I'm sorry to interrupt. Are you busy right now?

747
00:30:18,200 --> 00:30:22,200
I'm working on something, but I can take a quick break. What do you need?

748
00:30:22,200 --> 00:30:27,160
need. I wanted to ask if you could review my presentation before the meeting. Sure,

749
00:30:27,160 --> 00:30:32,560
I'd be happy to. When is your meeting? It's at 3 p.m. so anytime before that would

750
00:30:32,560 --> 00:30:38,320
be great. Okay, send it to me and I'll go through it in about 30 minutes. That would

751
00:30:38,320 --> 00:30:42,680
be amazing. Thank you so much. You're welcome. I'll give you feedback as soon

752
00:30:42,680 --> 00:30:48,360
as I'm done. Hey Daniel, can I ask you something? Of course, Sophia. Go ahead.

753
00:30:48,360 --> 00:30:52,360
I'm trying to book a meeting room, but the system isn't working for me.

754
00:30:52,360 --> 00:30:53,360
Do you know how to fix it?

755
00:30:53,360 --> 00:30:59,360
Yes, I've had that issue before. You need to refresh the page and log in again.

756
00:30:59,360 --> 00:31:01,360
Oh, really? Let me try that.

757
00:31:01,360 --> 00:31:05,360
If it still doesn't work, you can contact IT support.

758
00:31:05,360 --> 00:31:08,360
Okay, it's working now. Thank you for the tip.

759
00:31:08,360 --> 00:31:09,360
Glad I could help.

760
00:31:09,360 --> 00:31:11,360
Let's get started with the meeting.

761
00:31:11,360 --> 00:31:13,360
Good morning, everyone.

762
00:31:13,360 --> 00:31:15,360
Thank you all for joining today.

763
00:31:15,360 --> 00:31:19,360
Today we're going to discuss the new marketing strategy.

764
00:31:19,360 --> 00:31:23,360
If anyone has questions during the meeting, feel free to ask.

765
00:31:23,360 --> 00:31:26,360
Sophia, would you like to start with your presentation?

766
00:31:26,360 --> 00:31:31,360
Yes, thank you. I'd like to begin by showing last quarter's performance.

767
00:31:31,360 --> 00:31:33,360
Excuse me, can I add something?

768
00:31:33,360 --> 00:31:35,360
Of course, go ahead.

769
00:31:35,360 --> 00:31:40,360
I think it would also be helpful to compare this data with the previous year.

770
00:31:40,360 --> 00:31:43,360
That's a great idea. I'll include that in the next slide.

771
00:31:43,360 --> 00:31:44,360
Thank you.

772
00:31:44,360 --> 00:31:50,360
I see your point, Sophia, but I think we should also consider the budget limitations.

773
00:31:50,360 --> 00:31:54,360
That's true. Budget is definitely an important factor.

774
00:31:54,360 --> 00:31:57,360
Maybe we can find a balance between cost and impact.

775
00:31:57,360 --> 00:31:59,360
I agree with that approach.

776
00:31:59,360 --> 00:32:02,360
Great. I'm glad we're on the same page.

777
00:32:02,360 --> 00:32:05,360
Does anyone have any questions before we wrap up?

778
00:32:05,360 --> 00:32:07,360
I think everything is clear.

779
00:32:07,360 --> 00:32:14,360
Alright, to summarize, we agreed to move forward with the new strategy and adjust the budget accordingly.

780
00:32:14,360 --> 00:32:16,360
Thank you everyone for your time.

781
00:32:16,360 --> 00:32:18,360
Have a great day!

782
00:32:18,360 --> 00:32:20,360
Hey Sophia, are you going to lunch now?

783
00:32:20,360 --> 00:32:23,360
Yes, I am. Do you want to join me?

784
00:32:23,360 --> 00:32:26,360
Sure, that sounds great. Where are you going?

785
00:32:26,360 --> 00:32:29,360
I was thinking of trying that new café nearby.

786
00:32:29,360 --> 00:32:32,360
Oh, I've heard good things about it. Let's go.

787
00:32:32,360 --> 00:32:33,360
Perfect.

788
00:32:33,360 --> 00:32:34,360
This place looks nice.

789
00:32:34,360 --> 00:32:36,360
Yes, I like the atmosphere.

790
00:32:36,360 --> 00:32:38,360
What are you going to order?

791
00:32:38,360 --> 00:32:41,360
I'm thinking about getting a salad and a smoothie.

792
00:32:41,360 --> 00:32:44,360
Sounds healthy. I might get a sandwich.

793
00:32:44,360 --> 00:32:45,360
Good choice.

794
00:32:45,360 --> 00:32:47,360
So, how's your project going?

795
00:32:47,360 --> 00:32:50,360
It's going well, but it's quite challenging.

796
00:32:50,360 --> 00:32:53,360
I understand. Let me know if you need anything.

797
00:32:53,360 --> 00:32:55,360
Thank you. I appreciate that.

798
00:32:55,360 --> 00:32:57,360
That lunch looks delicious.

799
00:32:57,360 --> 00:32:59,360
Thanks. I made it myself.

800
00:32:59,360 --> 00:33:01,360
Really? That's impressive.

801
00:33:01,360 --> 00:33:04,360
Thank you. I enjoy cooking.

802
00:33:04,360 --> 00:33:06,360
Maybe you can teach me sometime.

803
00:33:06,360 --> 00:33:08,360
Sure, I'd love to.

804
00:33:08,360 --> 00:33:11,360
Sophia, great job on your presentation earlier.

805
00:33:11,360 --> 00:33:14,360
Thank you so much. I'm glad you liked it.

806
00:33:14,360 --> 00:33:16,360
It was very clear and well organized.

807
00:33:16,360 --> 00:33:18,360
I appreciate your feedback.

808
00:33:18,360 --> 00:33:21,360
You did an excellent job explaining the data.

809
00:33:21,360 --> 00:33:23,360
That means a lot. Thank you.

810
00:33:23,360 --> 00:33:26,360
I'm sorry for the delay in sending the report.

811
00:33:26,360 --> 00:33:28,360
That's okay. These things happen.

812
00:33:28,360 --> 00:33:30,360
I had some technical issues.

813
00:33:30,360 --> 00:33:33,360
No worries. I appreciate you letting me know.

814
00:33:33,360 --> 00:33:36,360
I'll make sure it doesn't happen again.

815
00:33:36,360 --> 00:33:38,360
Don't worry about it too much.

816
00:33:38,360 --> 00:33:40,360
Are you swamped today?

817
00:33:40,360 --> 00:33:42,360
Yes, I have a lot on my plate.

818
00:33:42,360 --> 00:33:45,360
Same here. It's been a busy week.

819
00:33:45,360 --> 00:33:47,360
Hopefully things will slow down soon.

820
00:33:47,360 --> 00:33:49,360
I hope so too.

821
00:33:49,360 --> 00:33:51,360
Do you want to grab a coffee?

822
00:33:51,360 --> 00:33:53,360
Sure, I could use a break.

823
00:33:53,360 --> 00:33:54,360
Let's go.

824
00:33:54,360 --> 00:33:55,360
Great idea.

825
00:33:55,360 --> 00:33:58,360
A few of us are going out for dinner after work.

826
00:33:58,360 --> 00:33:59,360
Do you want to join?

827
00:33:59,360 --> 00:34:02,360
That sounds nice, but I already have plans tonight.

828
00:34:02,360 --> 00:34:04,860
No problem. Maybe next time.

829
00:34:04,860 --> 00:34:06,860
Definitely. Thanks for inviting me.

830
00:34:06,860 --> 00:34:08,360
I'm heading out now.

831
00:34:08,360 --> 00:34:10,360
Alright. Have a great evening.

832
00:34:10,360 --> 00:34:12,360
You too. See you tomorrow.

833
00:34:12,360 --> 00:34:13,360
See ya.

834
00:34:13,360 --> 00:34:14,860
It's Friday today.

835
00:34:14,860 --> 00:34:16,360
Yes, finally.

836
00:34:16,360 --> 00:34:18,360
Any plans for the weekend?

837
00:34:18,360 --> 00:34:21,360
I'm going to visit my family. How about you?

838
00:34:21,360 --> 00:34:24,860
I'm planning to relax and maybe watch a movie.

839
00:34:24,860 --> 00:34:27,360
That sounds nice. Have a great weekend.

840
00:34:27,360 --> 00:34:29,360
You too. Enjoy your time.

841
00:34:29,360 --> 00:34:33,360
Hey Sophia, just wanted to follow up on our earlier discussion.

842
00:34:33,360 --> 00:34:34,360
Yes, go ahead.

843
00:34:34,360 --> 00:34:37,360
Have you had a chance to review the document?

844
00:34:37,360 --> 00:34:39,360
Not yet, but I will do it this afternoon.

845
00:34:39,360 --> 00:34:41,360
Okay, please keep me posted.

846
00:34:41,360 --> 00:34:42,360
I will.

847
00:34:42,360 --> 00:34:45,360
Let's touch base tomorrow morning about the project.

848
00:34:45,360 --> 00:34:47,360
That works for me.

849
00:34:47,360 --> 00:34:49,360
Great, I'll send you a calendar invite.

850
00:34:49,360 --> 00:34:50,360
Perfect.

851
00:34:50,360 --> 00:34:52,360
Can you swing by my desk later?

852
00:34:52,360 --> 00:34:54,360
Sure, what time?

853
00:34:54,360 --> 00:34:56,360
Around 2pm would be good.

854
00:34:56,360 --> 00:34:58,360
Okay, I'll be there.

855
00:34:58,360 --> 00:35:00,360
Let's catch up sometime this week.

856
00:35:00,360 --> 00:35:01,360
I'd like that.

857
00:35:01,360 --> 00:35:03,360
Maybe over coffee?

858
00:35:03,360 --> 00:35:04,360
Sounds great.

859
00:35:04,360 --> 00:35:06,360
This task is quite urgent.

860
00:35:06,360 --> 00:35:09,360
I understand. I'll prioritize it.

861
00:35:09,360 --> 00:35:11,360
Thank you. I appreciate it.

862
00:35:11,360 --> 00:35:12,360
No problem.

863
00:35:12,360 --> 00:35:15,360
I think we've covered everything for today.

864
00:35:15,360 --> 00:35:17,360
Yes, it was a productive discussion.

865
00:35:17,360 --> 00:35:19,360
Let's wrap up here.

866
00:35:19,360 --> 00:35:20,360
Agreed.

867
00:35:20,360 --> 00:35:22,360
That was a long day.

868
00:35:22,360 --> 00:35:24,360
Yes, but we got a lot done.

869
00:35:24,360 --> 00:35:26,360
Absolutely. Good teamwork.

870
00:35:26,360 --> 00:35:28,360
Absolutely.

871
00:35:28,360 --> 00:35:31,360
Talking with coworkers becomes easier with practice.

872
00:35:31,360 --> 00:35:35,360
Yes, the more you practice, the more confident you become.

873
00:35:35,360 --> 00:35:38,360
And remember to be polite, friendly, and respectful.

874
00:35:38,360 --> 00:35:43,360
Exactly. That's the key to good workplace communication.

875
00:35:43,360 --> 00:35:45,360
Thanks for joining us today.

876
00:35:45,360 --> 00:35:47,360
We hope you found this conversation helpful.

877
00:35:47,360 --> 00:35:49,360
Keep practicing every day.

878
00:35:49,360 --> 00:35:51,360
And don't be afraid to speak.

879
00:35:51,360 --> 00:35:53,360
See you next time.

880
00:35:53,360 --> 00:35:54,360
Goodbye.

881
00:35:54,360 --> 00:35:56,660
Welcome back to Business English Learning.

882
00:35:56,660 --> 00:36:00,300
Hi everyone, welcome to today's English Conversation Practice.

883
00:36:00,300 --> 00:36:01,140
I'm Daniel.

884
00:36:01,140 --> 00:36:07,220
And I'm Sophia, and we are here to help you speak English naturally and confidently at work.

885
00:36:07,220 --> 00:36:13,980
Today's topic is extremely practical, how to talk with co-workers in English in real-life situations.

886
00:36:13,980 --> 00:36:21,380
Yes, and this time we're going to go deeper, with longer, more natural, and more comprehensive conversations,

887
00:36:21,380 --> 00:36:23,460
just like real office life.

888
00:36:23,460 --> 00:36:29,180
Exactly. You'll hear how conversations flow throughout an entire workday, from morning

889
00:36:29,180 --> 00:36:30,180
to evening.

890
00:36:30,180 --> 00:36:33,540
All right, let's begin with the start of a typical workday.

891
00:36:33,540 --> 00:36:36,580
Hey, Sophia. Good morning. How are you doing today?

892
00:36:36,580 --> 00:36:41,160
Good morning, Daniel. I'm doing pretty well, thanks. I feel quite productive today. How

893
00:36:41,160 --> 00:36:42,160
about you?

894
00:36:42,160 --> 00:36:47,260
I'm doing okay, but I'm still a bit sleepy. I stayed up late finishing some work.

895
00:36:47,260 --> 00:36:50,740
Oh, that's tough. Did you at least finish everything?

896
00:36:50,740 --> 00:36:53,420
Yes, I did. So I feel relieved.

897
00:36:53,420 --> 00:36:57,260
That's good. Sometimes it's worth it if you complete your tasks.

898
00:36:57,260 --> 00:37:00,700
True. By the way, have you already had your coffee?

899
00:37:00,700 --> 00:37:04,620
Not yet, but I'm planning to grab one soon. Do you want to join me?

900
00:37:04,620 --> 00:37:07,060
That sounds great. I definitely need one.

901
00:37:07,060 --> 00:37:09,260
So Daniel, how was your weekend?

902
00:37:09,260 --> 00:37:13,900
It was quite relaxing. I didn't do much, just stayed home, watched a movie, and did

903
00:37:13,900 --> 00:37:14,900
some cleaning.

904
00:37:14,900 --> 00:37:19,300
That sounds nice. Sometimes doing nothing is the best way to recharge.

905
00:37:19,300 --> 00:37:21,220
Exactly. What about you?

906
00:37:21,220 --> 00:37:23,400
I actually went out with some friends.

907
00:37:23,400 --> 00:37:25,480
We tried a new restaurant in the city.

908
00:37:25,480 --> 00:37:26,640
Oh, really?

909
00:37:26,640 --> 00:37:27,640
Was the food good?

910
00:37:27,640 --> 00:37:29,440
Yes, it was amazing.

911
00:37:29,440 --> 00:37:31,360
You should definitely try it sometime.

912
00:37:31,360 --> 00:37:32,360
I will.

913
00:37:32,360 --> 00:37:33,360
Maybe next weekend.

914
00:37:33,360 --> 00:37:34,360
All right.

915
00:37:34,360 --> 00:37:35,960
I should start working on my tasks.

916
00:37:35,960 --> 00:37:38,600
I have quite a lot on my plate today.

917
00:37:38,600 --> 00:37:39,600
Same here.

918
00:37:39,600 --> 00:37:42,480
I have two meetings and a report to finish.

919
00:37:42,480 --> 00:37:44,280
Sounds like a busy day.

920
00:37:44,280 --> 00:37:45,280
Definitely.

921
00:37:45,280 --> 00:37:47,240
Hey, Sophia, do you have a minute?

922
00:37:47,240 --> 00:37:48,240
Sure.

923
00:37:48,240 --> 00:37:49,240
What's up?

924
00:37:49,240 --> 00:37:52,760
report, but I'm not sure how to organize the data section.

925
00:37:52,760 --> 00:37:53,760
Could you help me?

926
00:37:53,760 --> 00:37:54,760
Of course.

927
00:37:54,760 --> 00:37:56,600
Let me see what you have so far.

928
00:37:56,600 --> 00:37:57,600
Here it is.

929
00:37:57,600 --> 00:37:58,600
Okay.

930
00:37:58,600 --> 00:38:04,400
I think you can divide it into three parts, overview, analysis, and conclusion.

931
00:38:04,400 --> 00:38:05,400
That makes sense.

932
00:38:05,400 --> 00:38:07,320
I didn't think about splitting it like that.

933
00:38:07,320 --> 00:38:09,880
It will make your report much clearer.

934
00:38:09,880 --> 00:38:10,880
Thanks a lot.

935
00:38:10,880 --> 00:38:12,160
I really appreciate your help.

936
00:38:12,160 --> 00:38:13,160
No problem at all.

937
00:38:13,160 --> 00:38:15,600
Hey, Daniel, can I ask you something?

938
00:38:15,600 --> 00:38:16,600
Sure.

939
00:38:16,600 --> 00:38:20,480
Do you know who is responsible for the client presentation tomorrow?

940
00:38:20,480 --> 00:38:24,440
I think it's Mark, but I'm not 100% sure.

941
00:38:24,440 --> 00:38:27,040
Alright, I'll check with him, thanks.

942
00:38:27,040 --> 00:38:28,040
No problem.

943
00:38:28,040 --> 00:38:30,480
Hey, Sophia, are you free for a quick chat?

944
00:38:30,480 --> 00:38:32,400
I'm a bit swamped right now.

945
00:38:32,400 --> 00:38:34,400
Can we talk in 20 minutes?

946
00:38:34,400 --> 00:38:35,400
Of course.

947
00:38:35,400 --> 00:38:36,640
Just let me know when you're free.

948
00:38:36,640 --> 00:38:37,640
Will do.

949
00:38:37,640 --> 00:38:38,640
Thanks for understanding.

950
00:38:38,640 --> 00:38:40,600
Okay, Daniel, I'm free now.

951
00:38:40,600 --> 00:38:42,160
What did you want to discuss?

952
00:38:42,160 --> 00:38:45,000
I just wanted to talk about the project timeline.

953
00:38:45,000 --> 00:38:47,080
I feel like we're falling behind.

954
00:38:47,080 --> 00:38:49,200
Yeah, I've noticed that too.

955
00:38:49,200 --> 00:38:51,680
There's been a lot of unexpected work.

956
00:38:51,680 --> 00:38:52,600
Exactly.

957
00:38:52,600 --> 00:38:54,720
I think we need to adjust our plan.

958
00:38:54,720 --> 00:38:55,640
I agree.

959
00:38:55,640 --> 00:38:58,600
Maybe we should bring this up in the meeting later.

960
00:38:58,600 --> 00:38:59,520
Good idea.

961
00:38:59,520 --> 00:39:00,640
All right, everyone.

962
00:39:00,640 --> 00:39:02,640
Let's get started with the meeting.

963
00:39:02,640 --> 00:39:03,440
Good morning.

964
00:39:03,440 --> 00:39:05,760
Today, we'll review the project progress

965
00:39:05,760 --> 00:39:07,600
and discuss next steps.

966
00:39:07,600 --> 00:39:08,640
Sounds good.

967
00:39:08,640 --> 00:39:12,640
So far, we've completed about 70% of the work.

968
00:39:12,640 --> 00:39:14,640
Excuse me, can I add something?

969
00:39:14,640 --> 00:39:15,840
Of course.

970
00:39:15,840 --> 00:39:19,640
I think we might need more time to complete the remaining tasks.

971
00:39:19,640 --> 00:39:21,440
That's a valid point.

972
00:39:21,440 --> 00:39:24,840
I agree. The team has been quite busy with other priorities.

973
00:39:24,840 --> 00:39:29,240
I see your point, but we also need to meet the client's expectations.

974
00:39:29,240 --> 00:39:32,140
That's true. Maybe we can find a compromise.

975
00:39:32,140 --> 00:39:38,240
Yes. Perhaps we can extend the deadline slightly while focusing on key tasks first.

976
00:39:38,240 --> 00:39:39,940
That sounds like a good solution.

977
00:39:39,940 --> 00:39:41,940
Great. Is everyone on board?

978
00:39:41,940 --> 00:39:42,740
Yes.

979
00:39:42,740 --> 00:39:45,300
All right, let's move forward with that plan.

980
00:39:45,300 --> 00:39:47,140
I think that covers everything.

981
00:39:47,140 --> 00:39:49,300
Does anyone have any questions?

982
00:39:49,300 --> 00:39:50,820
No questions from me.

983
00:39:50,820 --> 00:39:53,340
All right, thank you everyone for your time.

984
00:39:53,340 --> 00:39:54,220
Thanks.

985
00:39:54,220 --> 00:39:56,140
That meeting was quite productive.

986
00:39:56,140 --> 00:39:59,540
Yes, I'm glad we discussed the issues openly.

987
00:39:59,540 --> 00:40:00,380
Me too.

988
00:40:00,380 --> 00:40:02,460
It helps avoid bigger problems later.

989
00:40:02,460 --> 00:40:03,740
Exactly.

990
00:40:03,740 --> 00:40:06,140
Hey, Sophia, are you free for lunch?

991
00:40:06,140 --> 00:40:07,020
Yes, I am.

992
00:40:07,020 --> 00:40:09,060
Do you want to grab something together?

993
00:40:09,060 --> 00:40:10,620
Sure, I need a break.

994
00:40:10,620 --> 00:40:11,820
Same here.

995
00:40:11,820 --> 00:40:15,260
So Daniel, how are you finding the project so far?

996
00:40:15,260 --> 00:40:17,340
It's challenging, but I'm learning a lot.

997
00:40:17,340 --> 00:40:18,220
That's good.

998
00:40:18,220 --> 00:40:20,020
Challenges help us grow.

999
00:40:20,020 --> 00:40:20,700
True.

1000
00:40:20,700 --> 00:40:21,620
What about you?

1001
00:40:21,620 --> 00:40:22,740
I feel the same.

1002
00:40:22,740 --> 00:40:24,700
It's busy, but interesting.

1003
00:40:24,700 --> 00:40:28,380
Hey, Sophia, that presentation earlier was really impressive.

1004
00:40:28,380 --> 00:40:29,540
Thank you so much.

1005
00:40:29,540 --> 00:40:31,020
I worked hard on it.

1006
00:40:31,020 --> 00:40:31,740
It shows.

1007
00:40:31,740 --> 00:40:33,740
You explained everything clearly.

1008
00:40:33,740 --> 00:40:35,100
I appreciate that.

1009
00:40:35,100 --> 00:40:39,140
Hey, Daniel, I'm sorry for the delay in sending you the files.

1010
00:40:39,140 --> 00:40:39,900
No worries.

1011
00:40:39,900 --> 00:40:41,220
Thanks for letting me know.

1012
00:40:41,220 --> 00:40:43,660
I had some issues with my computer.

1013
00:40:43,660 --> 00:40:44,500
That's okay.

1014
00:40:44,500 --> 00:40:45,740
These things happen.

1015
00:40:45,740 --> 00:40:49,060
Hey, Sophia, can you keep me posted on the client feedback?

1016
00:40:49,060 --> 00:40:49,900
Of course.

1017
00:40:49,900 --> 00:40:52,340
I'll update you as soon as I hear anything.

1018
00:40:52,340 --> 00:40:53,180
Thanks.

1019
00:40:53,180 --> 00:40:55,860
Hey, Daniel, just following up on the report,

1020
00:40:55,860 --> 00:40:56,940
did you finish it?

1021
00:40:56,940 --> 00:40:58,780
Yes, I sent it this morning.

1022
00:40:58,780 --> 00:40:59,740
Did you receive it?

1023
00:40:59,740 --> 00:41:00,660
Yes, I did.

1024
00:41:00,660 --> 00:41:01,780
It looks great.

1025
00:41:01,780 --> 00:41:02,660
Thanks.

1026
00:41:02,660 --> 00:41:04,700
Hey, Sophia, do you want to grab a coffee?

1027
00:41:04,700 --> 00:41:06,620
Sure, I could use a break.

1028
00:41:06,620 --> 00:41:09,340
I've been staring at my screen all afternoon.

1029
00:41:09,340 --> 00:41:12,020
Same here, a short break will help.

1030
00:41:12,020 --> 00:41:15,300
So Daniel, do you have any plans after work today?

1031
00:41:15,300 --> 00:41:17,740
Not really, I might just relax at home.

1032
00:41:17,740 --> 00:41:19,900
That sounds nice, what about you?

1033
00:41:19,900 --> 00:41:22,060
I actually meet a friend for dinner.

1034
00:41:22,060 --> 00:41:23,340
That sounds fun.

1035
00:41:23,340 --> 00:41:26,340
All right, I think I'm going to wrap up for today.

1036
00:41:26,340 --> 00:41:28,900
Same here, it's been a long day.

1037
00:41:28,900 --> 00:41:31,420
Definitely, good job today by the way.

1038
00:41:31,420 --> 00:41:32,860
Thanks, you too.

1039
00:41:32,860 --> 00:41:34,820
I really enjoy working with you.

1040
00:41:34,820 --> 00:41:37,620
Likewise, okay, I'm heading out now.

1041
00:41:37,620 --> 00:41:39,300
All right, have a great evening.

1042
00:41:39,300 --> 00:41:40,900
you too. See you tomorrow.

1043
00:41:40,900 --> 00:41:41,900
See you.

1044
00:41:41,900 --> 00:41:43,200
And if it's Friday…

1045
00:41:43,200 --> 00:41:44,300
Have a great weekend!

1046
00:41:44,300 --> 00:41:46,460
Thanks! Enjoy your weekend too.

1047
00:41:46,460 --> 00:41:47,660
See you on Monday.

1048
00:41:47,660 --> 00:41:50,860
See you. Wow, that felt like a real work day.

1049
00:41:50,860 --> 00:41:56,300
Yes, and all these conversations are natural and useful in everyday office life.

1050
00:41:56,300 --> 00:42:00,460
If you practice these patterns, you'll feel much more confident speaking with coworkers.

1051
00:42:00,460 --> 00:42:06,340
Remember, you don't need perfect English, just clear, polite, and friendly communication.

1052
00:42:06,340 --> 00:42:08,100
Keep practicing every day.

1053
00:42:08,100 --> 00:42:09,820
And don't be afraid to speak.

1054
00:42:09,820 --> 00:42:10,820
All right, everyone.

1055
00:42:10,820 --> 00:42:12,060
That's all for today.

1056
00:42:12,060 --> 00:42:15,300
Have a wonderful day and good luck with your workplace English.

1057
00:42:15,300 --> 00:42:16,300
Goodbye.

1058
00:42:16,300 --> 00:42:17,300
Bye.

1059
