with real-life, detailed conversations.

1065
00:42:36,300 --> 00:42:42,860
Yes, we'll walk through a full workday, from morning greetings to handling tasks, meetings,

1066
00:42:42,860 --> 00:42:45,980
challenges, and even after work interactions.

1067
00:42:45,980 --> 00:42:49,580
So let's begin with the start of the day at the office.

1068
00:42:49,580 --> 00:42:51,820
Good morning Tina, how are you today?

1069
00:42:51,820 --> 00:42:54,460
Good morning Leo, I'm doing well, thank you.

1070
00:42:54,460 --> 00:42:57,460
I feel quite focused today, how about you?

1071
00:42:57,460 --> 00:43:00,460
I'm doing okay, but I feel a bit rushed.

1072
00:43:00,460 --> 00:43:03,640
I had a lot of emails waiting for me this morning.

1073
00:43:03,640 --> 00:43:04,820
That happens a lot.

1074
00:43:04,820 --> 00:43:07,100
Mondays are especially busy, right?

1075
00:43:07,100 --> 00:43:08,700
Absolutely.

1076
00:43:08,700 --> 00:43:10,100
Did you have a good weekend?

1077
00:43:10,100 --> 00:43:11,300
Yes, I did.

1078
00:43:11,300 --> 00:43:15,260
I spent some time outdoors and also caught up on some reading.

1079
00:43:15,260 --> 00:43:16,260
What about you?

1080
00:43:16,260 --> 00:43:18,220
I mostly relaxed at home.

1081
00:43:18,220 --> 00:43:20,780
I needed that after a long week.

1082
00:43:20,780 --> 00:43:23,060
That sounds like a good way to recharge.

1083
00:43:23,060 --> 00:43:26,300
By the way, are you working on anything interesting today?

1084
00:43:26,300 --> 00:43:29,620
Yes, I'm preparing a presentation for a client meeting.

1085
00:43:29,620 --> 00:43:31,020
It's quite important.

1086
00:43:31,020 --> 00:43:32,020
What about you?

1087
00:43:32,020 --> 00:43:37,060
I'm finalizing a report and also joining a strategy meeting later.

1088
00:43:37,060 --> 00:43:38,980
Sounds like you have a full schedule.

1089
00:43:38,980 --> 00:43:39,980
Definitely.

1090
00:43:39,980 --> 00:43:42,100
All right, I'll let you get started.

1091
00:43:42,100 --> 00:43:43,100
Thanks.

1092
00:43:43,100 --> 00:43:44,100
Talk to you later.

1093
00:43:44,100 --> 00:43:45,660
Hey Tina, do you have a minute?

1094
00:43:45,660 --> 00:43:46,740
Sure, what's up?

1095
00:43:46,740 --> 00:43:51,140
I'm reviewing the project data and I noticed something doesn't look right.

1096
00:43:51,140 --> 00:43:52,580
Could you take a look with me?

1097
00:43:52,580 --> 00:43:53,580
Of course.

1098
00:43:53,580 --> 00:43:54,820
Let's go through it together.

1099
00:43:54,820 --> 00:43:59,820
I think the numbers from last week were updated, but this file still has the old

1100
00:43:59,820 --> 00:44:00,820
version.

1101
00:44:00,820 --> 00:44:05,820
Ah, I see the issue. We need to replace this section with the latest data.

1102
00:44:05,820 --> 00:44:08,820
That makes sense. Thanks for helping me catch that.

1103
00:44:08,820 --> 00:44:11,820
No problem. It's always good to double-check.

1104
00:44:11,820 --> 00:44:14,820
By the way, I really appreciate your attention to detail.

1105
00:44:14,820 --> 00:44:16,820
Thank you. That means a lot.

1106
00:44:16,820 --> 00:44:19,820
If you need help with your presentation later, just let me know.

1107
00:44:19,820 --> 00:44:21,820
I will. Thanks for offering.

1108
00:44:21,820 --> 00:44:26,820
Hey Tina, quick question. How do you usually structure your presentations?

1109
00:44:26,820 --> 00:44:33,820
I usually start with an introduction, then outline the key points, and finish with a summary and recommendations.

1110
00:44:33,820 --> 00:44:37,820
That's helpful. I sometimes struggle with the flow.

1111
00:44:37,820 --> 00:44:40,820
A good tip is to keep your message simple and clear.

1112
00:44:40,820 --> 00:44:42,820
I'll try that. Thanks.

1113
00:44:42,820 --> 00:44:43,820
Anytime.

1114
00:44:43,820 --> 00:44:45,820
Hey, are you heading to the meeting now?

1115
00:44:45,820 --> 00:44:48,820
Yes, it's about to start. Are you joining too?

1116
00:44:48,820 --> 00:44:50,820
Yes, let's go together.

1117
00:44:50,820 --> 00:44:51,820
Great.

1118
00:44:51,820 --> 00:44:53,820
Alright everyone, let's get started.

1119
00:44:53,820 --> 00:44:55,820
Thanks for joining everyone.

1120
00:44:55,820 --> 00:45:00,020
Today we'll discuss the project progress and next steps.

1121
00:45:00,020 --> 00:45:02,460
Leo, would you like to begin with the update?

1122
00:45:02,460 --> 00:45:03,460
Sure.

1123
00:45:03,460 --> 00:45:09,380
So far, we've completed most of the tasks, but we're slightly behind schedule.

1124
00:45:09,380 --> 00:45:11,740
Can you explain what caused the delay?

1125
00:45:11,740 --> 00:45:15,460
Mainly, some unexpected issues with data collection.

1126
00:45:15,460 --> 00:45:16,700
I see.

1127
00:45:16,700 --> 00:45:18,620
What do you suggest as a solution?

1128
00:45:18,620 --> 00:45:22,340
I think we should extend the deadline by two days.

1129
00:45:22,340 --> 00:45:23,840
That sounds reasonable.

1130
00:45:23,840 --> 00:45:24,840
What do you think?

1131
00:45:24,840 --> 00:45:29,840
I agree, but we should also improve our workflow to avoid future delays.

1132
00:45:29,840 --> 00:45:30,840
That's a good point.

1133
00:45:30,840 --> 00:45:33,840
Maybe we can assign clearer responsibilities.

1134
00:45:33,840 --> 00:45:35,840
I'm on board with that idea.

1135
00:45:35,840 --> 00:45:36,840
Great.

1136
00:45:36,840 --> 00:45:38,840
Does anyone else have suggestions?

1137
00:45:38,840 --> 00:45:39,840
I'd like to add something.

1138
00:45:39,840 --> 00:45:40,840
Go ahead.

1139
00:45:40,840 --> 00:45:44,840
We should also schedule regular check-ins to track progress.

1140
00:45:44,840 --> 00:45:45,840
That makes sense.

1141
00:45:45,840 --> 00:45:47,840
It will help us stay aligned.

1142
00:45:47,840 --> 00:45:49,840
All right, let's summarize.

1143
00:45:49,840 --> 00:45:53,840
We'll extend the deadline and improve communication.

1144
00:45:53,840 --> 00:45:54,900
Sounds good.

1145
00:45:54,900 --> 00:45:56,600
Any final questions?

1146
00:45:56,600 --> 00:45:57,740
None from me.

1147
00:45:57,740 --> 00:45:59,340
Okay, let's wrap up.

1148
00:45:59,340 --> 00:46:00,400
Thanks everyone.

1149
00:46:00,400 --> 00:46:01,240
Thank you.

1150
00:46:01,240 --> 00:46:02,900
That was a productive meeting.

1151
00:46:02,900 --> 00:46:05,300
Yes, I think we made good decisions.

1152
00:46:05,300 --> 00:46:07,240
Hey Tina, wanna grab lunch?

1153
00:46:07,240 --> 00:46:08,700
Sure, I'd love to.

1154
00:46:08,700 --> 00:46:09,940
Where should we go?

1155
00:46:09,940 --> 00:46:12,140
How about that new cafe nearby?

1156
00:46:12,140 --> 00:46:13,700
Sounds great, let's go.

1157
00:46:13,700 --> 00:46:15,300
This place looks nice.

1158
00:46:15,300 --> 00:46:17,340
Yes, I've heard good things about it.

1159
00:46:17,340 --> 00:46:20,640
So what do you usually do during your lunch break?

1160
00:46:20,640 --> 00:46:23,800
I like to relax and take a mental break from work.

1161
00:46:23,800 --> 00:46:27,240
Same here. It helps me stay productive in the afternoon.

1162
00:46:27,240 --> 00:46:28,360
Exactly.

1163
00:46:28,360 --> 00:46:30,520
Do you have any plans for the weekend?

1164
00:46:30,520 --> 00:46:33,400
I'm thinking about going hiking if the weather is good.

1165
00:46:33,400 --> 00:46:36,840
That sounds fun. I might just stay home and rest.

1166
00:46:36,840 --> 00:46:38,360
That's a good plan too.

1167
00:46:38,360 --> 00:46:39,720
Lunch was great.

1168
00:46:39,720 --> 00:46:41,160
Yes, I enjoyed it.

1169
00:46:41,160 --> 00:46:42,440
Back to work now.

1170
00:46:42,440 --> 00:46:43,400
Let's do it.

1171
00:46:43,400 --> 00:46:47,160
Hey Tina, I finished updating the report. Could you review it?

1172
00:46:47,160 --> 00:46:49,080
Sure. Give me a few minutes.

1173
00:46:49,080 --> 00:46:50,120
Take your time.

1174
00:46:50,120 --> 00:46:51,880
Okay, I've gone through it.

1175
00:46:51,880 --> 00:46:52,920
What do you think?

1176
00:46:52,920 --> 00:46:56,880
It looks very good overall, just a few small changes.

1177
00:46:56,880 --> 00:46:58,080
Please let me know.

1178
00:46:58,080 --> 00:47:02,640
The introduction could be shorter and one chart needs clarification.

1179
00:47:02,640 --> 00:47:04,400
Got it. I'll fix those.

1180
00:47:04,400 --> 00:47:05,520
Great work, though.

1181
00:47:05,520 --> 00:47:07,840
Thanks. I appreciate your feedback.

1182
00:47:07,840 --> 00:47:08,760
You're welcome.

1183
00:47:08,760 --> 00:47:12,560
Hey, Tina, I'm sorry I sent the wrong file earlier.

1184
00:47:12,560 --> 00:47:14,400
No worries. It happens.

1185
00:47:14,400 --> 00:47:16,400
I've sent the correct version now.

1186
00:47:16,400 --> 00:47:17,840
Thanks for updating me.

1187
00:47:17,840 --> 00:47:19,800
I'll be more careful next time.

1188
00:47:19,800 --> 00:47:21,680
It's okay. Don't worry about it.

1189
00:47:21,680 --> 00:47:25,520
By the way, are you free later to discuss tomorrow's meeting?

1190
00:47:25,520 --> 00:47:28,000
Yes, I'm available after 3pm.

1191
00:47:28,000 --> 00:47:29,760
Perfect. Let's meet then.

1192
00:47:29,760 --> 00:47:30,640
Sounds good.

1193
00:47:30,640 --> 00:47:34,160
All right. I think I'm done for today. I'm heading out.

1194
00:47:34,160 --> 00:47:35,760
Okay. Have a great evening.

1195
00:47:35,760 --> 00:47:37,600
You too. See you tomorrow.

1196
00:47:37,600 --> 00:47:38,400
See you.

1197
00:47:38,400 --> 00:47:42,160
Wow, Tina, that was a full day of conversations.

1198
00:47:42,160 --> 00:47:46,080
Yes, and we covered so many real workplace situations.

1199
00:47:46,080 --> 00:47:51,360
From greetings and small talk to meetings, feedback, and problem solving.

1200
00:47:51,360 --> 00:47:55,920
Exactly! These are the kinds of conversations you'll have every day at work.

1201
00:47:55,920 --> 00:47:58,480
What's the most important thing to remember?

1202
00:47:58,480 --> 00:48:01,200
Be polite, clear, and friendly.

1203
00:48:01,200 --> 00:48:03,200
And don't be afraid to speak.

1204
00:48:03,200 --> 00:48:06,080
Yes, practice is the key to improvement.

1205
00:48:06,080 --> 00:48:08,720
Even if you make mistakes, it's okay.

1206
00:48:08,720 --> 00:48:13,120
Absolutely. Communication is about understanding, not perfection.

1207
00:48:13,120 --> 00:48:19,120
Alright everyone, we hope this comprehensive conversation helps you feel more confident at work.

1208
00:48:19,120 --> 00:48:22,480
Keep practicing these phrases in your daily conversations.

1209
00:48:22,480 --> 00:48:23,680
Thanks for listening.

1210
00:48:23,680 --> 00:48:24,720
See you next time.

1211
00:48:24,720 --> 00:48:25,520
Goodbye.

1212
00:48:25,520 --> 00:48:26,240
Bye.

1213
00:48:26,240 --> 00:48:29,040
Welcome back to Business English Learning.

1214
00:48:29,040 --> 00:48:29,920
Hi everyone.

1215
00:48:29,920 --> 00:48:32,960
Welcome to today's English Conversation Practice.

1216
00:48:32,960 --> 00:48:33,920
I'm Daniel.

1217
00:48:33,920 --> 00:48:34,880
And I'm Sophia.

1218
00:48:34,880 --> 00:48:37,600
And we are here to help you speak English naturally

1219
00:48:37,600 --> 00:48:40,320
and confidently in real life situations.

1220
00:48:40,320 --> 00:48:44,240
Today we have a very practical and useful topic for you.

1221
00:48:44,240 --> 00:48:47,200
How to talk with co-workers in English.

1222
00:48:47,200 --> 00:48:51,960
Yes, this is something you will use every single day if you work in an office or any

1223
00:48:51,960 --> 00:48:53,560
professional environment.

1224
00:48:53,560 --> 00:48:54,800
Exactly.

1225
00:48:54,800 --> 00:49:01,160
You need to know how to greet people, make small talk, ask for help, and build good relationships.

1226
00:49:01,160 --> 00:49:05,920
And don't worry, we'll do everything through natural conversations with practical examples.

1227
00:49:05,920 --> 00:49:07,920
Alright, let's get started.

1228
00:49:07,920 --> 00:49:10,280
Let's imagine it's the beginning of a work day.

1229
00:49:10,280 --> 00:49:11,880
Hey Sophia, good morning.

1230
00:49:11,880 --> 00:49:12,880
How are you today?

1231
00:49:12,880 --> 00:49:13,880
Good morning Daniel.

1232
00:49:13,880 --> 00:49:14,880
I'm doing great.

1233
00:49:14,880 --> 00:49:15,880
Thanks.

1234
00:49:15,880 --> 00:49:16,880
How about you?

1235
00:49:16,880 --> 00:49:18,080
Just a bit tired.

1236
00:49:18,080 --> 00:49:19,480
I didn't sleep very well.

1237
00:49:19,480 --> 00:49:21,360
Oh no, you need more rest.

1238
00:49:21,360 --> 00:49:22,840
Maybe coffee will help.

1239
00:49:22,840 --> 00:49:23,640
Definitely.

1240
00:49:23,640 --> 00:49:25,280
I'm planning to get one soon.

1241
00:49:25,280 --> 00:49:28,000
That's how simple workplace conversations start.

1242
00:49:28,000 --> 00:49:30,000
Just greetings and small talk.

1243
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:30,880
Exactly.

1244
00:49:30,880 --> 00:49:32,120
Let's try another one.

1245
00:49:32,120 --> 00:49:32,720
Hey, Daniel.

1246
00:49:32,720 --> 00:49:33,440
Morning.

1247
00:49:33,440 --> 00:49:34,400
Morning, Sophia.

1248
00:49:34,400 --> 00:49:35,320
How's it going?

1249
00:49:35,320 --> 00:49:36,000
Pretty good.

1250
00:49:36,000 --> 00:49:37,800
Just getting ready for a busy day.

1251
00:49:37,800 --> 00:49:38,680
Same here.

1252
00:49:38,680 --> 00:49:41,000
Now let's imagine it's Monday.

1253
00:49:41,000 --> 00:49:41,840
Hey, Sophia.

1254
00:49:41,840 --> 00:49:43,000
How was your weekend?

1255
00:49:43,000 --> 00:49:43,760
It was great.

1256
00:49:43,760 --> 00:49:45,680
I relaxed and watched some movies.

1257
00:49:45,680 --> 00:49:46,600
What about you?

1258
00:49:46,600 --> 00:49:49,400
I went out with friends and had been here. It was fun.

1259
00:49:49,400 --> 00:49:50,520
That sounds nice.

1260
00:49:50,520 --> 00:49:54,040
This is one of the easiest ways to start conversations at work.

1261
00:49:54,040 --> 00:49:57,120
Yes. The weekend is always a safe topic.

1262
00:49:57,120 --> 00:49:59,640
Now let's move to asking for help.

1263
00:49:59,640 --> 00:50:01,360
Hey Daniel, do you have a minute?

1264
00:50:01,360 --> 00:50:02,520
Sure. What's up?

1265
00:50:02,520 --> 00:50:05,520
I'm having trouble with this document. Could you help me?

1266
00:50:05,520 --> 00:50:07,240
Of course. Let me take a look.

1267
00:50:07,240 --> 00:50:09,120
Thank you. I really appreciate it.

1268
00:50:09,120 --> 00:50:10,480
No problem at all.

1269
00:50:10,480 --> 00:50:12,680
Now what if someone is busy?

1270
00:50:12,680 --> 00:50:14,600
Hey Daniel, do you have a minute?

1271
00:50:14,600 --> 00:50:17,600
I'm a bit busy right now, can we talk later?

1272
00:50:17,600 --> 00:50:19,680
Sure, no problem, just let me know.

1273
00:50:19,680 --> 00:50:21,880
That's how you respect people's time.

1274
00:50:21,880 --> 00:50:24,800
Now, let's go into a meeting situation.

1275
00:50:24,800 --> 00:50:26,920
All right everyone, let's get started.

1276
00:50:26,920 --> 00:50:27,760
Good morning.

1277
00:50:27,760 --> 00:50:30,840
Today we're going to talk about the project timeline.

1278
00:50:30,840 --> 00:50:31,800
Sounds good.

1279
00:50:31,800 --> 00:50:34,320
First, let's review the deadlines.

1280
00:50:34,320 --> 00:50:36,200
Excuse me, can I add something?

1281
00:50:36,200 --> 00:50:37,080
Of course.

1282
00:50:37,080 --> 00:50:39,680
I think we should consider the team's workload.

1283
00:50:39,680 --> 00:50:40,960
That's a good point.

1284
00:50:40,960 --> 00:50:41,840
I agree.

1285
00:50:41,840 --> 00:50:45,000
Now let's practice disagreeing politely.

1286
00:50:45,000 --> 00:50:48,480
I see your point, but I think we need to move faster.

1287
00:50:48,480 --> 00:50:49,800
That's understandable.

1288
00:50:49,800 --> 00:50:52,120
Maybe we can find a middle solution.

1289
00:50:52,120 --> 00:50:53,480
Yes, that works.

1290
00:50:53,480 --> 00:50:54,800
Now lunch time.

1291
00:50:54,800 --> 00:50:56,760
Hey, Sophia, are you free for lunch?

1292
00:50:56,760 --> 00:50:57,600
Yes, I am.

1293
00:50:57,600 --> 00:50:59,360
Do you want to grab something together?

1294
00:50:59,360 --> 00:51:00,560
Sure, let's go.

1295
00:51:00,560 --> 00:51:02,320
What if I say no?

1296
00:51:02,320 --> 00:51:03,800
Hey, Sophia, lunch?

1297
00:51:03,800 --> 00:51:05,800
I'd love to, but I have a meeting.

1298
00:51:05,800 --> 00:51:06,920
Maybe tomorrow?

1299
00:51:06,920 --> 00:51:07,720
Of course.

1300
00:51:07,720 --> 00:51:09,240
Now in the kitchen.

1301
00:51:09,240 --> 00:51:10,960
Hey, Daniel, making coffee?

1302
00:51:10,960 --> 00:51:12,760
Yes, I need it today.

1303
00:51:12,760 --> 00:51:13,800
Same here.

1304
00:51:13,800 --> 00:51:15,760
That lunch looks delicious.

1305
00:51:15,760 --> 00:51:16,520
Thanks.

1306
00:51:16,520 --> 00:51:18,040
Now, compliments.

1307
00:51:18,040 --> 00:51:19,960
Great job on the presentation.

1308
00:51:19,960 --> 00:51:21,280
Thank you so much.

1309
00:51:21,280 --> 00:51:22,720
You did really well.

1310
00:51:22,720 --> 00:51:23,920
I appreciate it.

1311
00:51:23,920 --> 00:51:25,840
Now, apologizing.

1312
00:51:25,840 --> 00:51:27,440
I'm sorry for the delay.

1313
00:51:27,440 --> 00:51:28,320
That's OK.

1314
00:51:28,320 --> 00:51:29,760
Thanks for understanding.

1315
00:51:29,760 --> 00:51:30,520
Of course.

1316
00:51:30,520 --> 00:51:31,840
End of the day.

1317
00:51:31,840 --> 00:51:32,880
I'm heading out.

1318
00:51:32,880 --> 00:51:33,920
See you tomorrow.

1319
00:51:33,920 --> 00:51:34,880
Have a good evening.

1320
00:51:34,880 --> 00:51:35,760
You too.

1321
00:51:35,760 --> 00:51:37,080
Friday version.

1322
00:51:37,080 --> 00:51:38,360
Have a great weekend.

1323
00:51:38,360 --> 00:51:38,920
Thanks.

1324
00:51:38,920 --> 00:51:39,680
You too.

1325
00:51:39,680 --> 00:51:41,780
Now a longer conversation.

1326
00:51:41,780 --> 00:51:43,640
Hey Sophia, do you have a moment?

1327
00:51:43,640 --> 00:51:45,120
Sure, what's going on?

1328
00:51:45,120 --> 00:51:47,680
I feel like we're behind on the project.

1329
00:51:47,680 --> 00:51:49,960
I agree, there's a lot to do.

1330
00:51:49,960 --> 00:51:52,080
I'm a bit worried about the deadline.

1331
00:51:52,080 --> 00:51:54,360
Me too, let's talk to the manager.

1332
00:51:54,360 --> 00:51:55,320
Good idea.

1333
00:51:55,320 --> 00:51:56,680
I'll schedule a meeting.

1334
00:51:56,680 --> 00:51:57,520
Thanks.

1335
00:51:57,520 --> 00:51:58,480
In the meeting.

1336
00:51:58,480 --> 00:51:59,600
Thanks for joining.

1337
00:51:59,600 --> 00:52:01,440
We need help with workload.

1338
00:52:01,440 --> 00:52:03,640
Understood, let's adjust the plan.

1339
00:52:03,640 --> 00:52:05,760
That would help, after meeting.

1340
00:52:05,760 --> 00:52:06,840
That went well.

1341
00:52:06,840 --> 00:52:07,680
Yes.

1342
00:52:07,680 --> 00:52:08,680
Coffee break.

1343
00:52:08,680 --> 00:52:09,880
Want to grab coffee?

1344
00:52:09,880 --> 00:52:10,600
Sure.

1345
00:52:10,600 --> 00:52:11,680
I need a break.

1346
00:52:11,680 --> 00:52:12,680
Same here.

1347
00:52:12,680 --> 00:52:13,680
Back to work.

1348
00:52:13,680 --> 00:52:15,520
Keep me posted on updates.

1349
00:52:15,520 --> 00:52:16,400
Will do.

1350
00:52:16,400 --> 00:52:17,440
Follow up.

1351
00:52:17,440 --> 00:52:19,560
Just following up on my email.

1352
00:52:19,560 --> 00:52:20,880
I'll reply soon.

1353
00:52:20,880 --> 00:52:21,880
Teamwork.

1354
00:52:21,880 --> 00:52:23,440
Let's catch up quickly.

1355
00:52:23,440 --> 00:52:24,120
Sure.

1356
00:52:24,120 --> 00:52:26,720
You do the report, I'll do the slides.

1357
00:52:26,720 --> 00:52:27,600
Perfect.

1358
00:52:27,600 --> 00:52:28,920
Encouragement.

1359
00:52:28,920 --> 00:52:30,280
You're doing great.

1360
00:52:30,280 --> 00:52:31,240
Thank you.

1361
00:52:31,240 --> 00:52:32,560
We'll finish this.

1362
00:52:32,560 --> 00:52:33,960
Yes, together.

1363
00:52:33,960 --> 00:52:36,480
That was a lot of useful conversation.

1364
00:52:36,480 --> 00:52:38,520
Yes, and all of it is practical

1365
00:52:38,520 --> 00:52:40,500
for real work situations.

1366
00:52:40,500 --> 00:52:42,980
Just remember to be polite and friendly.

1367
00:52:42,980 --> 00:52:44,660
And don't be afraid to speak.

1368
00:52:44,660 --> 00:52:46,220
Practice every day.

1369
00:52:46,220 --> 00:52:47,880
You'll improve naturally.

1370
00:52:47,880 --> 00:52:48,860
Goodbye, everyone.

1371
00:52:48,860 --> 00:52:54,040
Bye.

1372
00:52:54,040 --> 00:52:56,520
Welcome back to Business English Learning.

1373
00:52:56,520 --> 00:52:57,360
Hi, everyone.

1374
00:52:57,360 --> 00:53:00,280
Welcome to today's English Conversation Practice.

1375
00:53:00,280 --> 00:53:01,280
I'm Daniel.

1376
00:53:01,280 --> 00:53:02,360
And I'm Sophia.

1377
00:53:02,360 --> 00:53:05,120
And we are here to help you speak English naturally

1378
00:53:05,120 --> 00:53:07,720
and confidently in real-life situations.

1379
00:53:07,720 --> 00:53:11,320
Today we have a very practical and useful topic for you,

1380
00:53:11,320 --> 00:53:14,020
how to talk with co-workers in English.

1381
00:53:14,020 --> 00:53:17,160
Yes, this is something you will use every single day

1382
00:53:17,160 --> 00:53:20,440
if you work in an office or any professional environment.

1383
00:53:20,440 --> 00:53:21,280
That's right.

1384
00:53:21,280 --> 00:53:24,620
Talking with co-workers is not just about work tasks.

1385
00:53:24,620 --> 00:53:26,800
It's also about building relationships,

1386
00:53:26,800 --> 00:53:29,440
being polite and communicating clearly.

1387
00:53:29,440 --> 00:53:30,280
Exactly.

1388
00:53:30,280 --> 00:53:33,520
In today's lesson, we'll go through many natural conversations

1389
00:53:33,520 --> 00:53:36,600
you can use at work, from greetings and small talk

1390
00:53:36,600 --> 00:53:39,660
to asking for help, meetings and casual chats.

1391
00:53:39,660 --> 00:53:42,380
And remember, the goal is not perfection.

1392
00:53:42,380 --> 00:53:46,020
The goal is communication, so don't be afraid to speak.

1393
00:53:46,020 --> 00:53:47,080
Absolutely.

1394
00:53:47,080 --> 00:53:50,060
All right, let's get started with our first situation.

1395
00:53:50,060 --> 00:53:51,260
Good morning, Sophia.

1396
00:53:51,260 --> 00:53:52,300
How are you today?

1397
00:53:52,300 --> 00:53:53,340
Good morning, Daniel.

1398
00:53:53,340 --> 00:53:54,660
I'm doing well, thank you.

1399
00:53:54,660 --> 00:53:55,580
How about you?

1400
00:53:55,580 --> 00:53:56,420
I'm good.

1401
00:53:56,420 --> 00:53:57,980
Just a bit busy this morning.

1402
00:53:57,980 --> 00:53:58,900
I understand.

1403
00:53:58,900 --> 00:54:01,180
Mornings can be hectic sometimes.

1404
00:54:01,180 --> 00:54:03,820
Yes, I have a few deadlines today.

1405
00:54:03,820 --> 00:54:05,060
That sounds like a lot.

1406
00:54:05,060 --> 00:54:06,820
Let me know if you need any help.

1407
00:54:06,820 --> 00:54:07,660
Thanks.

1408
00:54:07,660 --> 00:54:08,540
I appreciate that.

1409
00:54:08,540 --> 00:54:10,620
Hey Sophia, how was your weekend?

1410
00:54:10,620 --> 00:54:11,900
It was really nice.

1411
00:54:11,900 --> 00:54:14,500
I spent some time with my family and relaxed.

1412
00:54:14,500 --> 00:54:15,460
How about you?

1413
00:54:15,460 --> 00:54:16,300
Pretty good.

1414
00:54:16,300 --> 00:54:18,860
I watched a movie and caught up on some sleep.

1415
00:54:18,860 --> 00:54:20,780
That sounds like a perfect weekend.

1416
00:54:20,780 --> 00:54:21,580
It was.

1417
00:54:21,580 --> 00:54:23,620
I feel more refreshed now.

1418
00:54:23,620 --> 00:54:24,460
That's great.

1419
00:54:24,460 --> 00:54:25,820
Ready for a new week?

1420
00:54:25,820 --> 00:54:27,540
As ready as I can be.

1421
00:54:27,540 --> 00:54:29,540
Hi Sophia, do you have a minute?

1422
00:54:29,540 --> 00:54:30,040
Sure.

1423
00:54:30,040 --> 00:54:30,780
What's up?

1424
00:54:30,780 --> 00:54:32,820
I need some help with this report.

1425
00:54:32,820 --> 00:54:34,980
I'm not sure if I'm doing it correctly.

1426
00:54:34,980 --> 00:54:35,860
No problem.

1427
00:54:35,860 --> 00:54:36,980
Let me take a look.

1428
00:54:36,980 --> 00:54:38,980
Thanks, I really appreciate it.

1429
00:54:38,980 --> 00:54:40,740
Okay, I see what you mean.

1430
00:54:40,740 --> 00:54:43,100
You just need to adjust this section.

1431
00:54:43,100 --> 00:54:44,460
Oh, I see now.

1432
00:54:44,460 --> 00:54:45,500
That makes sense.

1433
00:54:45,500 --> 00:54:46,860
It's an easy fix.

1434
00:54:46,860 --> 00:54:48,260
Thanks again for your help.

1435
00:54:48,260 --> 00:54:50,860
Sophia, could you explain this part to me?

1436
00:54:50,860 --> 00:54:51,700
Of course.

1437
00:54:51,700 --> 00:54:53,380
Which part are you referring to?

1438
00:54:53,380 --> 00:54:54,900
This section here.

1439
00:54:54,900 --> 00:54:56,700
I don't fully understand it.

1440
00:54:56,700 --> 00:54:59,540
Okay, let me walk you through it step by step.

1441
00:54:59,540 --> 00:55:00,700
That would be great.

1442
00:55:00,700 --> 00:55:02,900
First, you need to analyze the data,

1443
00:55:02,900 --> 00:55:04,900
then summarize your findings.

1444
00:55:04,900 --> 00:55:05,620
Got it.

1445
00:55:05,620 --> 00:55:06,900
That helps a lot.

1446
00:55:06,900 --> 00:55:08,100
I'm glad it does.

1447
00:55:08,100 --> 00:55:10,580
Hey Sophia, are you free for lunch today?

1448
00:55:10,580 --> 00:55:11,900
I think so.

1449
00:55:11,900 --> 00:55:13,340
What time were you thinking?

1450
00:55:13,340 --> 00:55:14,820
Around 1 PM.

1451
00:55:14,820 --> 00:55:15,900
That works for me.

1452
00:55:15,900 --> 00:55:16,420
Great.

1453
00:55:16,420 --> 00:55:18,660
Do you want to try the new cafe in your buy?

1454
00:55:18,660 --> 00:55:19,160
Sure.

1455
00:55:19,160 --> 00:55:20,420
I've heard it's really good.

1456
00:55:20,420 --> 00:55:20,980
Perfect.

1457
00:55:20,980 --> 00:55:21,980
Let's go together.

1458
00:55:21,980 --> 00:55:23,180
Looking forward to it.

1459
00:55:23,180 --> 00:55:25,980
Sophia, can I ask your opinion on something?

1460
00:55:25,980 --> 00:55:26,580
Of course.

1461
00:55:26,580 --> 00:55:27,420
Go ahead.

1462
00:55:27,420 --> 00:55:30,980
I'm thinking about changing the layout of this presentation.

1463
00:55:30,980 --> 00:55:32,540
That could be a good idea.

1464
00:55:32,540 --> 00:55:33,900
What do you have in mind?

1465
00:55:33,900 --> 00:55:37,900
Maybe adding more visuals and fewer text slides?

1466
00:55:37,900 --> 00:55:40,400
I like that. It will make it more engaging.

1467
00:55:40,400 --> 00:55:42,200
Great. I'll work on that.

1468
00:55:42,200 --> 00:55:44,200
Let me know if you want feedback later.

1469
00:55:44,200 --> 00:55:46,400
Hey, Sophia. Are you busy right now?

1470
00:55:46,400 --> 00:55:49,100
A little bit. I'm finishing something urgent.

1471
00:55:49,100 --> 00:55:51,200
No problem. I can come back later.

1472
00:55:51,200 --> 00:55:53,800
Thanks. Give me about 15 minutes.

1473
00:55:53,800 --> 00:55:55,200
Sure. That works.

1474
00:55:55,200 --> 00:55:56,800
I'll let you know when I'm free.

1475
00:55:56,800 --> 00:55:58,000
Perfect. Thank you.

1476
00:55:58,000 --> 00:56:00,500
Sophia, great job on the meeting today.

1477
00:56:00,500 --> 00:56:01,900
Thank you so much.

1478
00:56:01,900 --> 00:56:04,980
Your presentation was really clear and professional.

1479
00:56:04,980 --> 00:56:06,100
I appreciate that.

1480
00:56:06,100 --> 00:56:07,340
I worked hard on it.

1481
00:56:07,340 --> 00:56:08,900
It definitely showed.

1482
00:56:08,900 --> 00:56:09,740
That means a lot.

1483
00:56:09,740 --> 00:56:10,540
Thank you.

1484
00:56:10,540 --> 00:56:11,460
Hi, Sophia.

1485
00:56:11,460 --> 00:56:13,060
I'm sorry for the delay.

1486
00:56:13,060 --> 00:56:13,820
That's OK.

1487
00:56:13,820 --> 00:56:15,700
I was just about to check in with you.

1488
00:56:15,700 --> 00:56:18,260
I had some unexpected issues this morning.

1489
00:56:18,260 --> 00:56:19,100
No worries.

1490
00:56:19,100 --> 00:56:20,340
Do you need more time?

1491
00:56:20,340 --> 00:56:22,940
I think I can finish it by the end of the day.

1492
00:56:22,940 --> 00:56:23,940
That sounds good.

1493
00:56:23,940 --> 00:56:25,300
Thanks for understanding.

1494
00:56:25,300 --> 00:56:28,420
Sophia, do you know who is handling this project?

1495
00:56:28,420 --> 00:56:31,220
I believe it's John from the marketing team.

1496
00:56:31,220 --> 00:56:33,340
Oh, okay. I'll reach out to him.

1497
00:56:33,340 --> 00:56:35,420
Good idea. He should have the details.

1498
00:56:35,420 --> 00:56:36,860
Thanks for the information.

1499
00:56:36,860 --> 00:56:37,700
Anytime.

1500
00:56:37,700 --> 00:56:41,300
Hey, Sophia, can we talk about the project timeline?

1501
00:56:41,300 --> 00:56:44,540
Yes, we should. It's important to stay on track.

1502
00:56:44,540 --> 00:56:46,900
I think we might need more time.

1503
00:56:46,900 --> 00:56:49,300
I agree. Let's discuss it with the team.

1504
00:56:49,300 --> 00:56:50,180
Good plan.

1505
00:56:50,180 --> 00:56:52,100
We can bring it up in the next meeting.

1506
00:56:52,100 --> 00:56:54,340
Sophia, do you want to grab a coffee?

1507
00:56:54,340 --> 00:56:56,860
I'd love to, but I have a meeting soon.

1508
00:56:56,860 --> 00:56:58,540
No problem. Maybe later?

1509
00:56:58,540 --> 00:57:00,540
Yes. Maybe in the afternoon.

1510
00:57:00,540 --> 00:57:01,460
Sounds good.

1511
00:57:01,460 --> 00:57:02,340
See you then.

1512
00:57:02,340 --> 00:57:04,540
Hey, Sophia, I'm heading out now.

1513
00:57:04,540 --> 00:57:06,140
All right, have a great evening.

1514
00:57:06,140 --> 00:57:07,660
You too, see you tomorrow.

1515
00:57:07,660 --> 00:57:08,500
See you.

1516
00:57:08,500 --> 00:57:10,580
Sophia, thanks for your help today.

1517
00:57:10,580 --> 00:57:12,340
You're welcome, happy to help.

1518
00:57:12,340 --> 00:57:13,980
I couldn't have done it without you.

1519
00:57:13,980 --> 00:57:15,540
I'm glad I could support you.

1520
00:57:15,540 --> 00:57:17,140
It really made a difference.

1521
00:57:17,140 --> 00:57:18,420
That's great to hear.

1522
00:57:18,420 --> 00:57:20,020
Sophia, before we finish,

1523
00:57:20,020 --> 00:57:21,940
is there anything else we need to do?

1524
00:57:21,940 --> 00:57:23,780
I think we've covered everything.

1525
00:57:23,780 --> 00:57:25,500
Great, let's wrap it up then.

1526
00:57:25,500 --> 00:57:26,420
Sounds good.

1527
00:57:26,420 --> 00:57:27,500
Thanks for your time.

1528
00:57:27,500 --> 00:57:28,620
Thank you as well.

1529
00:57:28,620 --> 00:57:31,720
And that's the end of today's conversation practice.

1530
00:57:31,720 --> 00:57:34,320
We hope these examples help you feel more confident

1531
00:57:34,320 --> 00:57:36,100
when talking with your coworkers.

1532
00:57:36,100 --> 00:57:38,820
Remember to be polite, friendly, and clear.

1533
00:57:38,820 --> 00:57:42,020
And most importantly, keep practicing every day.

1534
00:57:42,020 --> 00:57:43,140
Thanks for listening.

1535
00:57:43,140 --> 00:57:48,730
See you next time.

1536
00:57:48,730 --> 00:57:50,610
Hello, everyone, and welcome back

1537
00:57:50,610 --> 00:57:52,890
to our English Learning Podcast.

1538
00:57:52,890 --> 00:57:53,810
I'm Leo.

1539
00:57:53,810 --> 00:57:55,090
And I'm Tina.

1540
00:57:55,090 --> 00:57:57,650
We're here to help you speak English naturally

1541
00:57:57,650 --> 00:57:59,330
and confidently at work.

1542
00:57:59,330 --> 00:58:02,130
Today we have a very important topic,

1543
00:58:02,130 --> 00:58:06,930
How to talk with co-workers in English using real-life conversations.

1544
00:58:06,930 --> 00:58:13,330
Yes, this is something you do every day at work so it's essential to sound polite, friendly, and natural.

1545
00:58:13,330 --> 00:58:20,830
Exactly. We'll go through many practical examples from greetings to meetings, small talk, to problem solving.

1546
00:58:20,830 --> 00:58:24,830
So, if you're ready, let's start with a typical morning at the office.

1547
00:58:24,830 --> 00:58:27,030
Good morning, Tina. How are you today?

1548
00:58:27,030 --> 00:58:30,430
Good morning, Leo. I'm doing well. Thank you. How about you?

1549
00:58:30,430 --> 00:58:34,830
I'm good. Just a bit busy already. I have a lot on my plate today.

1550
00:58:34,830 --> 00:58:38,350
Same here. It looks like it's going to be a productive day.

1551
00:58:38,350 --> 00:58:40,510
Did you have a good evening yesterday?

1552
00:58:40,510 --> 00:58:44,430
Yes, it was nice. I relaxed and watched a movie. What about you?

1553
00:58:44,430 --> 00:58:47,390
I just stayed home and caught up on some work.

1554
00:58:47,390 --> 00:58:49,150
Sounds like a calm evening.

1555
00:58:49,150 --> 00:58:53,950
So after greeting coworkers, we usually move to small talk, right?

1556
00:58:53,950 --> 00:58:59,070
Exactly. Small talk helps build relationships and makes the workplace more comfortable.

1557
00:58:59,070 --> 00:59:01,710
What are some easy small talk questions?

1558
00:59:01,710 --> 00:59:05,950
You can ask, how was your weekend or any plans today?

1559
00:59:05,950 --> 00:59:08,990
Let's try that. Hey Tina, how was your weekend?

1560
00:59:08,990 --> 00:59:12,510
It was great. I spent time with family. How about yours?

1561
00:59:12,510 --> 00:59:15,790
Mine was relaxing. I didn't do much, just rested.

1562
00:59:15,790 --> 00:59:17,230
That sounds perfect.

1563
00:59:17,230 --> 00:59:21,150
Now let's move to a work situation. I need help from you.

1564
00:59:21,150 --> 00:59:22,510
Okay, go ahead.

1565
00:59:22,510 --> 00:59:25,310
Hey Tina, do you have a minute to discuss something?

1566
00:59:25,310 --> 00:59:26,750
Sure, what's going on?

1567
00:59:26,750 --> 00:59:30,590
I noticed an issue in the report, the numbers don't match.

1568
00:59:30,590 --> 00:59:33,230
Oh, thanks for letting me know. I'll check it.

1569
00:59:33,230 --> 00:59:36,430
I just wanted to make sure we fix it before sending it.

1570
00:59:36,430 --> 00:59:38,510
Good catch. I appreciate it.

1571
00:59:38,510 --> 00:59:41,310
That's how you raise a concern politely.

1572
00:59:41,310 --> 00:59:44,430
Yes, focus on the issue, not the person.

1573
00:59:44,430 --> 00:59:46,990
Now let's talk about giving feedback.

1574
00:59:46,990 --> 00:59:47,950
Go ahead.

1575
00:59:47,950 --> 00:59:51,870
Tina, your presentation was really clear and well organized.

1576
00:59:51,870 --> 00:59:53,870
Thank you. I'm glad you think so.

1577
00:59:53,870 --> 00:59:56,990
One suggestion. Maybe add more examples.

1578
00:59:56,990 --> 00:59:58,990
That's helpful. I'll improve that.

1579
00:59:58,990 --> 01:00:02,030
See? Positive first, then suggestion.

1580
01:00:02,030 --> 01:00:03,230
Exactly.

1581
01:00:03,230 --> 01:00:04,830
Now, meetings.

1582
01:00:04,830 --> 01:00:06,510
Very important topic.

1583
01:00:06,510 --> 01:00:08,990
I'll write everyone. Let's get started.

1584
01:00:08,990 --> 01:00:11,070
Thanks for joining. Let's begin.

1585
01:00:11,070 --> 01:00:13,230
Excuse me. Can I add something?

1586
01:00:13,230 --> 01:00:14,030
Go ahead.

1587
01:00:14,030 --> 01:00:16,430
I think we should adjust the timeline.

1588
01:00:16,430 --> 01:00:17,790
That's a good point.

1589
01:00:17,790 --> 01:00:19,470
What if you disagree?

1590
01:00:19,470 --> 01:00:22,670
I see your point, but I have a different opinion.

1591
01:00:22,670 --> 01:00:23,710
That's polite.

1592
01:00:23,710 --> 01:00:31,230
Always be respectful now lunchtime my favorite part. Hey Tina want to grab lunch? Sure. Let's go

1593
01:00:31,430 --> 01:00:37,830
Where should we go? Maybe the new restaurant nearby sounds good at lunch. You can talk about hobbies

1594
01:00:38,070 --> 01:00:45,390
Do you have plans this weekend? I might go hiking. What about you? I'll probably relax at home nice and simple

1595
01:00:45,870 --> 01:00:48,170
Now declining invitations

1596
01:00:48,170 --> 01:00:53,570
important skill. Do you want to join us for dinner? Thanks, but I have plans tonight.

1597
01:00:53,570 --> 01:00:57,810
That's polite. Yes, no need to explain too much. Now,

1598
01:00:57,810 --> 01:01:05,330
apologizing. Go ahead. I'm sorry for the delay. No worries. Apologies for being late. That's

1599
01:01:05,330 --> 01:01:11,610
okay. Now, appreciation. Very important. Thanks for your help today. You're welcome.

1600
01:01:11,610 --> 01:01:20,170
I really appreciate your support happy to help now end of day. Let's wrap up. I'm heading out. Have a good evening

1601
01:01:20,530 --> 01:01:26,450
See you tomorrow. Take care on Friday. Have a great weekend. You too. Perfect

1602
01:01:26,730 --> 01:01:34,570
Let's do one full day conversation. Good idea. Morning Tina. Morning Leo. How are you doing? Well? Thanks

1603
01:01:34,570 --> 01:01:40,910
Do you have a minute? Sure. Could you review my report? Of course. Thanks. No problem

1604
01:01:40,910 --> 01:01:42,910
Later, did you check it?

1605
01:01:42,910 --> 01:01:44,410
Yes, looks good.

1606
01:01:44,410 --> 01:01:45,910
Any suggestions?

1607
01:01:45,910 --> 01:01:47,410
Just minor changes.

1608
01:01:47,410 --> 01:01:48,410
I'll fix them.

1609
01:01:48,410 --> 01:01:48,910
Great.

1610
01:01:48,910 --> 01:01:49,410
Lunch.

1611
01:01:49,410 --> 01:01:50,410
Let's go.

1612
01:01:50,410 --> 01:01:51,410
That was nice.

1613
01:01:51,410 --> 01:01:53,410
Yes, very relaxing.

1614
01:01:53,410 --> 01:01:54,410
End of day.

1615
01:01:54,410 --> 01:01:55,410
Heading out.

1616
01:01:55,410 --> 01:01:56,410
Have a good evening.

1617
01:01:56,410 --> 01:01:57,410
See you tomorrow.

1618
01:01:57,410 --> 01:01:58,410
See you.

1619
01:01:58,410 --> 01:02:01,910
So Tina, what's the key to talking with coworkers?

1620
01:02:01,910 --> 01:02:03,910
Be polite, clear and friendly.

1621
01:02:03,910 --> 01:02:05,910
And practice every day.

1622
01:02:05,910 --> 01:02:07,410
Exactly.

1623
01:02:07,410 --> 01:02:09,410
Alright everyone, thanks for listening.

1624
01:02:09,410 --> 01:02:12,170
Keep practicing your English at work.

1625
01:02:12,170 --> 01:02:13,170
See you next time.

1626
01:02:13,170 --> 01:02:14,170
Goodbye.

1627
01:02:14,170 --> 01:02:17,010
Welcome back to Business English Learning.

1628
01:02:17,010 --> 01:02:18,010
Hi everyone.

1629
01:02:18,010 --> 01:02:21,570
Welcome to today's English Conversation Practice.

1630
01:02:21,570 --> 01:02:22,890
I'm Daniel.

1631
01:02:22,890 --> 01:02:24,250
And I'm Sophia.

1632
01:02:24,250 --> 01:02:30,450
And we're here to help you speak English naturally and confidently in real life situations.

1633
01:02:30,450 --> 01:02:34,610
Today we have a very practical and useful topic for you.

1634
01:02:34,610 --> 01:02:37,490
How to talk with coworkers in English.

1635
01:02:37,490 --> 01:02:42,730
Yes, this is something you will use every single day if you work in an office or any

1636
01:02:42,730 --> 01:02:44,750
professional environment.

1637
01:02:44,750 --> 01:02:47,550
At work, you don't just speak English.

1638
01:02:47,550 --> 01:02:51,790
You communicate, build relationships, and work as a team.

1639
01:02:51,790 --> 01:02:55,930
Exactly, and sometimes the hardest part is not grammar.

1640
01:02:55,930 --> 01:02:59,370
It's knowing what to say in real situations.

1641
01:02:59,370 --> 01:03:05,590
So today, we'll show you natural conversations you can use at work right away.

1642
01:03:05,590 --> 01:03:10,910
Let's start with a very common situation, arriving at the office in the morning.

1643
01:03:10,910 --> 01:03:11,910
Good morning!

1644
01:03:11,910 --> 01:03:12,910
How are you today?

1645
01:03:12,910 --> 01:03:13,910
Good morning!

1646
01:03:13,910 --> 01:03:14,910
I'm doing well.

1647
01:03:14,910 --> 01:03:15,910
Thanks.

1648
01:03:15,910 --> 01:03:16,910
How about you?

1649
01:03:16,910 --> 01:03:17,910
I'm good.

1650
01:03:17,910 --> 01:03:18,910
Just a bit sleepy today.

1651
01:03:18,910 --> 01:03:20,270
I didn't sleep enough last night.

1652
01:03:20,270 --> 01:03:22,670
Oh no, that happens.

1653
01:03:22,670 --> 01:03:24,670
Maybe you need an extra coffee.

1654
01:03:24,670 --> 01:03:25,670
Definitely.

1655
01:03:25,670 --> 01:03:28,870
I think I'll grab one right after I sit down.

1656
01:03:28,870 --> 01:03:29,870
Same here.

1657
01:03:29,870 --> 01:03:32,310
So, how was your evening yesterday?

1658
01:03:32,310 --> 01:03:33,750
It was pretty relaxing.

1659
01:03:33,750 --> 01:03:36,470
I stayed home and watched a series.

1660
01:03:36,470 --> 01:03:37,470
How about you?

1661
01:03:37,470 --> 01:03:39,110
I had a busy evening.

1662
01:03:39,110 --> 01:03:42,430
I finished some work and replied to emails.

1663
01:03:42,430 --> 01:03:43,430
Sounds productive.

1664
01:03:43,430 --> 01:03:46,470
Yeah, a little too productive, actually.

1665
01:03:46,470 --> 01:03:50,350
By the way, did you see the message about the team meeting today?

1666
01:03:50,350 --> 01:03:51,990
Yes, I did.

1667
01:03:51,990 --> 01:03:53,910
It's at 10.30, right?

1668
01:03:53,910 --> 01:03:54,910
That's right.

1669
01:03:54,910 --> 01:03:55,910
Are you ready for it?

1670
01:03:55,910 --> 01:03:56,910
Almost.

1671
01:03:56,910 --> 01:03:59,070
I still need to review my notes.

1672
01:03:59,070 --> 01:04:00,070
Same here.

1673
01:04:00,070 --> 01:04:03,270
Let's go through it before the meeting if we have time.

1674
01:04:03,270 --> 01:04:04,270
Good idea.

1675
01:04:04,270 --> 01:04:05,450
Hey, excuse me.

1676
01:04:05,450 --> 01:04:06,450
Do you have a minute?

1677
01:04:06,450 --> 01:04:07,450
Sure.

1678
01:04:07,450 --> 01:04:08,450
What's up?

1679
01:04:08,450 --> 01:04:12,270
I'm working on this report and I'm a bit confused about one part.

1680
01:04:12,270 --> 01:04:13,270
Could you help me?

1681
01:04:13,270 --> 01:04:14,270
Of course.

1682
01:04:14,270 --> 01:04:15,270
Let me take a look.

1683
01:04:15,270 --> 01:04:16,270
Thanks.

1684
01:04:16,270 --> 01:04:17,270
I really appreciate it.

1685
01:04:17,270 --> 01:04:18,270
No problem.

1686
01:04:18,270 --> 01:04:19,270
Okay.

1687
01:04:19,270 --> 01:04:23,710
I think this section needs more explanation and a clear example.

1688
01:04:23,710 --> 01:04:25,350
Oh, I see.

1689
01:04:25,350 --> 01:04:26,630
That makes sense.

1690
01:04:26,630 --> 01:04:29,630
And maybe add a short summary at the end.

1691
01:04:29,630 --> 01:04:31,350
That's a great suggestion.

1692
01:04:31,350 --> 01:04:32,350
You're welcome.

1693
01:04:32,350 --> 01:04:34,830
By the way, are you free for lunch today?

1694
01:04:34,830 --> 01:04:35,830
I think so.

1695
01:04:35,830 --> 01:04:37,550
Do you want to grab something together?

1696
01:04:37,550 --> 01:04:39,230
Yes, that would be nice.

1697
01:04:39,230 --> 01:04:40,230
Great.

1698
01:04:40,230 --> 01:04:41,230
Where should we go?

1699
01:04:41,230 --> 01:04:43,390
There's a new cafe near the office.

1700
01:04:43,390 --> 01:04:44,510
Have you tried it?

1701
01:04:44,510 --> 01:04:46,910
Not yet, but I've heard good things about it.

1702
01:04:46,910 --> 01:04:47,910
Perfect.

1703
01:04:47,910 --> 01:04:48,910
Let's try it then.

1704
01:04:48,910 --> 01:04:49,910
Sounds good.

1705
01:04:49,910 --> 01:04:52,030
Hey, I have a quick question for you.

1706
01:04:52,030 --> 01:04:53,030
Sure.

1707
01:04:53,030 --> 01:04:55,430
Are you going to the meeting this afternoon?

1708
01:04:55,430 --> 01:04:56,430
Yes I am.

1709
01:04:56,430 --> 01:04:57,430
Why?

1710
01:04:57,430 --> 01:05:00,510
I'm a bit nervous about speaking in the meeting.

1711
01:05:00,510 --> 01:05:01,510
Don't worry.

1712
01:05:01,510 --> 01:05:03,370
it simple and clear.

1713
01:05:03,370 --> 01:05:05,230
That's easier said than done.

1714
01:05:05,230 --> 01:05:08,690
True, but you can prepare a few key points.

1715
01:05:08,690 --> 01:05:09,850
Good idea.

1716
01:05:09,850 --> 01:05:11,350
Maybe I should practice.

1717
01:05:11,350 --> 01:05:13,770
Yes, I can help you if you want.

1718
01:05:13,770 --> 01:05:15,330
That would be really helpful.

1719
01:05:15,330 --> 01:05:17,250
Okay, let's try.

1720
01:05:17,250 --> 01:05:18,970
What do you want to say?

1721
01:05:18,970 --> 01:05:23,450
Maybe something like, excuse me, I'd like to share an update.

1722
01:05:23,450 --> 01:05:24,450
Perfect.

1723
01:05:24,450 --> 01:05:26,410
That sounds very professional.

1724
01:05:26,410 --> 01:05:29,090
And then I explain my idea, right?

1725
01:05:29,090 --> 01:05:30,090
Exactly.

1726
01:05:30,090 --> 01:05:32,590
Speak slowly and confidently.

1727
01:05:32,590 --> 01:05:35,070
What if someone disagrees with me?

1728
01:05:35,070 --> 01:05:40,970
You can say, I understand your point, but I think that keeps it polite.

1729
01:05:40,970 --> 01:05:42,850
That sounds really useful.

1730
01:05:42,850 --> 01:05:44,010
It is.

1731
01:05:44,010 --> 01:05:46,610
Politeness is very important at work.

1732
01:05:46,610 --> 01:05:47,610
Definitely.

1733
01:05:47,610 --> 01:05:52,770
Okay, let's continue with another situation, working on a project deadline.

1734
01:05:52,770 --> 01:05:55,730
Oh yes, deadlines can be stressful.

1735
01:05:55,730 --> 01:05:59,170
Hey, I just got an email from the manager.

1736
01:05:59,170 --> 01:06:00,290
What does it say?

1737
01:06:00,290 --> 01:06:03,290
The report needs to be finished by tomorrow morning.

1738
01:06:03,290 --> 01:06:04,930
Wow, that's urgent.

1739
01:06:04,930 --> 01:06:08,730
Yes, a bit stressful. Are you okay with that?

1740
01:06:08,730 --> 01:06:11,370
I think so, but I may need some help.

1741
01:06:11,370 --> 01:06:13,330
Sure, we can work on it together.

1742
01:06:13,330 --> 01:06:15,930
Thanks, I really appreciate it.

1743
01:06:15,930 --> 01:06:18,490
No problem. Teamwork makes it easier.

1744
01:06:18,490 --> 01:06:19,490
Absolutely.

1745
01:06:19,490 --> 01:06:23,730
Hey, how do you usually write emails to coworkers?

1746
01:06:23,730 --> 01:06:28,770
I keep it simple. I start with hi or hello and their name.

1747
01:06:28,770 --> 01:06:32,770
Then I clearly explain what I need or what I'm updating.

1748
01:06:32,770 --> 01:06:35,770
And I always try to be polite and direct.

1749
01:06:35,770 --> 01:06:39,770
Yes, and I end with thanks or best regards.

1750
01:06:39,770 --> 01:06:40,770
That's a good habit.

1751
01:06:40,770 --> 01:06:43,770
Okay, let's imagine we are in the office kitchen.

1752
01:06:43,770 --> 01:06:46,770
That's where the best small talk happens.

1753
01:06:46,770 --> 01:06:48,770
Hey, that looks good. What are you having?

1754
01:06:48,770 --> 01:06:50,770
I brought lunch from home today.

1755
01:06:50,770 --> 01:06:52,770
Nice, it smells great.

1756
01:06:52,770 --> 01:06:54,770
Thanks. What about you?

1757
01:06:54,770 --> 01:06:57,770
I'm planning to order something. Any suggestions?

1758
01:06:57,770 --> 01:07:01,770
There's a good place nearby that serves really good noodles.

1759
01:07:01,770 --> 01:07:03,770
Sounds perfect. I'll try that.

1760
01:07:03,770 --> 01:07:04,770
Good choice.

1761
01:07:04,770 --> 01:07:06,770
Hey, do you need a hand with that?

1762
01:07:06,770 --> 01:07:09,770
Yes, please. That would be great.

1763
01:07:09,770 --> 01:07:10,770
No problem.

1764
01:07:10,770 --> 01:07:11,770
Thanks for your help.

1765
01:07:11,770 --> 01:07:12,770
Anytime.

1766
01:07:12,770 --> 01:07:15,770
Now let's move to the end of the workday.

1767
01:07:15,770 --> 01:07:18,770
Yes, saying goodbye is also important.

1768
01:07:18,770 --> 01:07:20,770
I'm heading out now.

1769
01:07:20,770 --> 01:07:21,770
Okay, have a good evening.

1770
01:07:21,770 --> 01:07:23,770
Thanks, you too.

1771
01:07:23,770 --> 01:07:24,770
See you tomorrow.

1772
01:07:24,770 --> 01:07:25,770
See you.

1773
01:07:25,770 --> 01:07:28,770
And if it's Friday, we can say something special.

1774
01:07:28,770 --> 01:07:30,770
Right. Have a great weekend.

1775
01:07:30,770 --> 01:07:31,770
Exactly.

1776
01:07:31,770 --> 01:07:34,770
And on Monday, we ask, how was your weekend?

1777
01:07:34,770 --> 01:07:37,770
It's a simple but natural cycle.

1778
01:07:37,770 --> 01:07:44,770
Before we finish, remember this. Communication at work is about being polite, clear and friendly.

1779
01:07:44,770 --> 01:07:48,770
Yes, don't worry about perfect English. Focus on connection.

1780
01:07:48,770 --> 01:07:52,770
Mistakes are okay. What matters is communication.

1781
01:07:52,770 --> 01:07:53,770
Absolutely.

1782
01:07:53,770 --> 01:07:54,770
Absolutely.

1783
01:07:54,770 --> 01:07:57,730
Keep practicing these phrases every day.

1784
01:07:57,730 --> 01:08:00,810
And use them with your co-workers in real life.

1785
01:08:00,810 --> 01:08:02,570
Thanks for listening, everyone.

1786
01:08:02,570 --> 01:08:04,130
We'll see you in the next lesson.

1787
01:08:04,130 --> 01:08:05,130
Goodbye.

1788
01:08:05,130 --> 01:08:05,650
Bye, everyone.
